ENTRY 9533 {"id":9533,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"# pi-durable-k8s\n\nRun [Pi Durable](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi) coding agents on your own Kubernetes cluster.\n\nEach session gets an agent that keeps its state in PostgreSQL and resumes after a crash, plus a private gVisor\nsandbox with a persistent workspace where its tools run. Model and GitHub credentials never reach the agent or the\nsandbox: [OneCLI](https://github.com/onecli/onecli) injects them at its gateway.\n\n**Status: proof of concept.** It runs end to end on a small arm64 lab cluster. It is not hardened for production;\nsee the open items in [plan.md](plan.md).\n\n![Architecture](docs/architecture.svg)\n\n## How it works\n\n1. A client creates a session and posts messages to the **session API** (`packages/ingest`).\n2. Messages land in an inbox in **PostgreSQL** first, so nothing is lost while the agent is busy or restarting.\n3. The **orchestrator** (`packages/orchestrator`) runs one durable Pi agent loop per session and takes inbox\n   messages in order.\n4. Model calls go through the **OneCLI gateway**, which adds the subscription or API key on the way out.\n5. Tool calls (bash, read, write, edit) run in the session's **sandbox**: a pod from\n   [agent-sandbox](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/agent-sandbox) under gVisor, with the `pi-env` daemon inside.\n   It is created on the first tool call and keeps its workspace on a PVC.\n6. Progress and answers stream back to the client over SSE.\n\nOptionally a session works on one GitHub repository: the orchestrator mints a token scoped to that repository,\nstores it in OneCLI for that session only, and the sandbox clones and pushes through the gateway.\n\n## Security model\n\n- Sandboxes run under gVisor. Network policies (written for Cilium) block sandboxes from the orchestrator, the\n  database, the Kubernetes API, OneCLI's management API and each other.\n- Each sandbox's daemon accepts only its own token, derived from a master key the orchestrator holds\n  ([ADR 0001](docs/decisions/0001-per-sandbox-sandboxd-token.md)).\n- No credentials in sandboxes or in the agent: OneCLI holds them and only relays to allowlisted hosts\n  ([host rules](docs/onecli-host-rules.md)).\n\n## Repository layout\n\n| Path                                   | What                                                                                                 |\n| -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `packages/ingest`                      | Session API: auth, owner checks, inbox writes, SSE proxy                                             |\n| `packages/orchestrator`                | Pi Durable harness, sandbox lifecycle, model and OneCLI wiring                                       |\n| `packages/sandbox-env`                 | Bridge from Pi's `RemoteExecutionEnv` to an agent-sandbox pod (the only SDK user)                    |\n| `packages/session-core`                | Shared schema, migrations and auth helpers                                                           |\n| `packages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client` | Vendored, pinned agent-sandbox TypeScript SDK (Apache-2.0)                                           |\n| `vendor/`                              | Packed `@netzlabor/pi-durable-postgres` adapter, ported to Pi Durable 1.5.2                          |\n| `images/sandbox`                       | Sandbox image: sandboxd + `pi-env` + git                                                             |\n| `deploy/`                              | Kubernetes manifests (namespace, Postgres, orchestrator, ingest, sandbox template, network policies) |\n| `tests/e2e`                            | End-to-end suites that run as in-cluster Jobs                                                        |\n| `docs/`                                | API, credentials, networking, decisions and research notes                                           |\n\n## Docs\n\n- [Session API](docs/session-api.md)\n- [Model credentials through OneCLI](docs/model-credentials.md)\n- [Repository workspaces](docs/repo-workspace.md)\n- [Network policy](docs/network-policy.md) and [OneCLI host rules](docs/onecli-host-rules.md)\n- [Plan, decisions and phase results](plan.md)\n\n## Development\n\nRequires Node 22.19+ and pnpm.\n\n```sh\npnpm install\npnpm check        # build, lint, format, typecheck, unit tests\ntests/e2e/run.sh smoke   # needs a cluster with agent-sandbox, gVisor and the deploy/ manifests applied\n```\n\n## License\n\nMIT, see [LICENSE](LICENSE). The vendored agent-sandbox SDK in `packages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client` keeps its Apache-2.0 license.\n---FILES---\npackages/ingest/src/main.ts\npackages/ingest/src/config.ts\npackages/ingest/src/events.ts\npackages/ingest/src/server.ts\npackages/ingest/src/log.ts\npackages/session-core/src/store.ts\npackages/session-core/src/db.ts\npackages/session-core/src/models.ts\npackages/session-core/src/repo.ts\npackages/session-core/src/http.ts\npackages/session-core/src/migrate.ts\npackages/session-core/src/auth.ts\npackages/session-core/src/index.ts\npackages/session-core/migrations/003_reasoning.sql\npackages/session-core/migrations/002_models.sql\npackages/session-core/migrations/001_inbox.sql\npackages/session-core/migrations/004_repo.sql\npackages/session-core/migrations/005_exec_in_flight.sql\npackages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/onecli.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/providers.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/stream.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/watcher.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/model.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/lifecycle.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/host.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/config.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/storage.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/kube.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/failure.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/github-app.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/sweeper.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/http.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/bridge-launcher.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/sweep.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/log.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/inbox.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/workspace.ts\npackages/orchestrator/src/onecli-admin.ts\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 9537 {"id":9537,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"","calls":["bash({\"command\":\"cd /workspace/repo && for f in packages/ingest/src/{server,events,config}.ts packages/session-core/src/{auth,http,store,repo,models,migrate}.ts packages/orchestrator/src/http.ts packages/session-core/migrations/*.sql; do echo =====$f; nl -ba \\\"$f\\\"; done\",\"timeout\":10000})"]}]}
ENTRY 9543 {"id":9543,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"   147\t  const repo = chooseRepo(body);\n   148\t  if (typeof repo === \"string\") {\n   149\t    sendJson(res, 400, { error: repo });\n   150\t    return;\n   151\t  }\n   152\t  const sessionId = await createSession(deps.pool, principal, model, repo);\n   153\t  sendJson(res, 201, {\n   154\t    sessionId,\n   155\t    provider: model.provider,\n   156\t    model: model.model,\n   157\t    ...(model.reasoning === undefined ? {} : { reasoning: model.reasoning }),\n   158\t    ...(repo === undefined\n   159\t      ? {}\n   160\t      : { repo: repo.repo, ...(repo.branch === undefined ? {} : { branch: repo.branch }) }),\n   161\t  });\n   162\t}\n   163\t\n   164\tasync function ownedSession(\n   165\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   166\t  id: string,\n   167\t  principal: Principal,\n   168\t): Promise<SessionRow | undefined> {\n   169\t  if (!UUID.test(id)) return undefined;\n   170\t  const session = await getSession(pool, id);\n   171\t  return session?.ownerSubject === principal.subject ? session : undefined;\n   172\t}\n   173\t\n   174\tasync function postEvent(\n   175\t  req: IncomingMessage,\n   176\t  res: ServerResponse,\n   177\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   178\t  session: SessionRow,\n   179\t  principal: Principal,\n   180\t): Promise<void> {\n   181\t  let parsed;\n   182\t  try {\n   183\t    parsed = parseEventBody(await readJsonObject(req));\n   184\t  } catch (error) {\n   185\t    if (error instanceof BodyError) {\n   186\t      sendJson(res, 400, { error: error.message });\n   187\t      return;\n   188\t    }\n   189\t    throw error;\n   190\t  }\n   191\t  if (typeof parsed === \"string\") {\n   192\t    sendJson(res, 400, { error: parsed });\n   193\t    return;\n   194\t  }\n   195\t  if (session.status !== \"active\") {\n   196\t    sendJson(res, session.status === \"deleted\" ? 410 : 409, {\n   197\t      error: `session is ${session.status}`,\n   198\t    });\n   199\t    return;\n   200\t  }\n   201\t  const result = await enqueueEvent(pool, {\n   202\t    sessionId: session.id,\n   203\t    source: `api:${principal.owner}`,\n   204\t    sourceEventId: parsed.sourceEventId,\n   205\t    kind: parsed.kind,\n   206\t    payload: parsed.payload,\n   207\t  });\n   208\t  if (result.outcome === \"conflict\") {\n   209\t    sendJson(res, 409, { error: \"sourceEventId was already used for another session\" });\n   210\t    return;\n   211\t  }\n   212\t  // 202 either way: a repeated post is accepted and names the first event.\n   213\t  sendJson(res, 202, { eventId: result.eventId, duplicate: result.outcome === \"duplicate\" });\n   214\t}\n   215\t\n   216\tasync function queueDelete(\n   217\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   218\t  session: SessionRow,\n   219\t  principal: Principal,\n   220\t  res: ServerResponse,\n   221\t): Promise<void> {\n   222\t  if (session.status === \"deleted\") {\n   223\t    sendJson(res, 202, { sessionId: session.id, status: \"deleted\" });\n   224\t    return;\n   225\t  }\n   226\t  // The delete is an inbox row like any other, so it runs after the events accepted before it.\n   227\t  const result = await enqueueEvent(pool, {\n   228\t    sessionId: session.id,\n   229\t    source: `api:${principal.owner}`,\n   230\t    sourceEventId: `delete:${session.id}`,\n   231\t    kind: \"delete\",\n   232\t    payload: {},\n   233\t  });\n   234\t  await requestDelete(pool, session.id);\n   235\t  const eventId = result.outcome === \"conflict\" ? undefined : result.eventId;\n   236\t  sendJson(res, 202, { sessionId: session.id, status: \"deleting\", eventId });\n   237\t}\n   238\t\n   239\t/**\n   240\t * Pipes the orchestrator's SSE stream to the client. The orchestrator authenticates the same token again.\n   241\t * When the upstream ends (orchestrator restart) the client's response ends too; the client reconnects\n   242\t * with Last-Event-ID and resumes.\n   243\t */\n   244\tfunction proxyStream(\n   245\t  req: IncomingMessage,\n   246\t  res: ServerResponse,\n   247\t  orchestratorUrl: string,\n   248\t  sessionId: string,\n   249\t): void {\n   250\t  const target = new URL(`/sessions/${sessionId}/stream`, orchestratorUrl);\n   251\t  const headers: Record<string, string> = { accept: \"text/event-stream\" };\n   252\t  if (typeof req.headers.authorization === \"string\")\n   253\t    headers.authorization = req.headers.authorization;\n   254\t  const lastEventId = req.headers[\"last-event-id\"];\n   255\t  if (typeof lastEventId === \"string\") headers[\"last-event-id\"] = lastEventId;\n   256\t\n   257\t  const upstream = httpRequest(target, { method: \"GET\", headers }, (up) => {\n   258\t    const type = up.headers[\"content-type\"];\n   259\t    res.writeHead(up.statusCode ?? 502, {\n   260\t      \"content-type\": typeof type === \"string\" ? type : \"application/json\",\n   261\t      \"cache-control\": \"no-cache\",\n   262\t      \"x-accel-buffering\": \"no\",\n   263\t    });\n   264\t    up.pipe(res);\n   265\t    up.on(\"error\", () => res.end());\n   266\t  });\n   267\t  upstream.on(\"error\", () => {\n   268\t    if (!res.headersSent) {\n   269\t      sendJson(res, 503, { error: \"orchestrator unavailable, retry\" }, { \"retry-after\": \"2\" });\n   270\t    } else {\n   271\t      res.end();\n   272\t    }\n   273\t  });\n   274\t  res.on(\"close\", () => upstream.destroy());\n   275\t  // The orchestrator sends a keepalive every 15 s. Silence for 45 s means it is gone without closing the\n   276\t  // connection (node lost, network cut): drop the stream so the client reconnects instead of waiting forever.\n   277\t  upstream.setTimeout(45_000, () => upstream.destroy());\n   278\t  upstream.end();\n   279\t}\n=====packages/ingest/src/events.ts\n     1\timport { randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\n     2\timport type { EventKind } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n     3\t\n     4\tconst MAX_TEXT = 64 * 1024;\n     5\tconst MAX_SOURCE_EVENT_ID = 200;\n     6\t\n     7\texport interface ParsedEvent {\n     8\t  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \"delete\">;\n     9\t  payload: { text?: string };\n    10\t  sourceEventId: string;\n    11\t}\n    12\t\n    13\t/** Validates the body of POST /sessions/{id}/events. Returns an error string for the 400 response. */\n    14\texport function parseEventBody(body: Record<string, unknown>): ParsedEvent | string {\n    15\t  const { kind, text, sourceEventId } = body;\n    16\t  if (kind === \"delete\") return \"use DELETE /sessions/{id} to delete a session\";\n    17\t  if (kind !== \"message\" && kind !== \"steer\" && kind !== \"cancel\") {\n    18\t    return \"kind must be message, steer or cancel\";\n    19\t  }\n    20\t  if (kind !== \"cancel\") {\n    21\t    if (typeof text !== \"string\" || text.trim() === \"\") return `${kind} needs a non-empty text`;\n    22\t    if (text.length > MAX_TEXT) return `text is longer than ${String(MAX_TEXT)} characters`;\n    23\t  } else if (text !== undefined) {\n    24\t    return \"cancel takes no text\";\n    25\t  }\n    26\t  if (sourceEventId !== undefined) {\n    27\t    if (\n    28\t      typeof sourceEventId !== \"string\" ||\n    29\t      sourceEventId === \"\" ||\n    30\t      sourceEventId.length > MAX_SOURCE_EVENT_ID\n    31\t    ) {\n    32\t      return `sourceEventId must be a string of 1 to ${String(MAX_SOURCE_EVENT_ID)} characters`;\n    33\t    }\n    34\t  }\n    35\t  return {\n    36\t    kind,\n    37\t    payload: typeof text === \"string\" ? { text } : {},\n    38\t    // Without a client-supplied id every post is its own event: there is nothing to deduplicate on.\n    39\t    sourceEventId: typeof sourceEventId === \"string\" ? sourceEventId : `auto-${randomUUID()}`,\n    40\t  };\n    41\t}\n=====packages/ingest/src/config.ts\n     1\timport { loadModelPolicy } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n     2\timport type { ModelPolicy } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n     3\t\n     4\t/** Environment contract of ingest. The database URL and the API tokens are secrets: env-only, never logged. */\n     5\texport interface IngestConfig {\n     6\t  databaseUrl: string;\n     7\t  /** `owner:token` entries, see session-core `tokenAuthenticator`. */\n     8\t  apiTokens: string;\n     9\t  /** Base URL of the orchestrator's stream endpoint. */\n    10\t  orchestratorUrl: string;\n    11\t  port: number;\n    12\t  instance: string;\n    13\t  /** Default model and allowlist for POST /sessions (same variables as the orchestrator, from one ConfigMap). */\n    14\t  models: ModelPolicy;\n    15\t}\n    16\t\n    17\texport function loadConfig(env: Readonly<Record<string, string | undefined>>): IngestConfig {\n    18\t  const databaseUrl = env.PI_DURABLE_DATABASE_URL;\n    19\t  if (!databaseUrl) throw new Error(\"PI_DURABLE_DATABASE_URL is required\");\n    20\t  const apiTokens = env.PI_API_TOKENS;\n    21\t  if (!apiTokens) throw new Error(\"PI_API_TOKENS is required\");\n    22\t  const port = Number(env.PI_INGEST_PORT ?? \"8080\");\n    23\t  if (!Number.isInteger(port) || port < 0 || port > 65535) {\n    24\t    throw new Error(\"PI_INGEST_PORT is invalid\");\n    25\t  }\n    26\t  return {\n    27\t    databaseUrl,\n    28\t    apiTokens,\n    29\t    orchestratorUrl: env.PI_ORCH_URL ?? \"http://pi-orchestrator:8081\",\n    30\t    port,\n    31\t    instance: env.POD_NAME ?? `ingest-${String(process.pid)}`,\n    32\t    models: loadModelPolicy(env),\n    33\t  };\n    34\t}\n=====packages/session-core/src/auth.ts\n     1\timport { createHash, timingSafeEqual } from \"node:crypto\";\n     2\timport type { IncomingHttpHeaders } from \"node:http\";\n     3\t\n     4\t/** Who is calling. `owner` is recorded on every session and checked on every call. */\n     5\texport interface Principal {\n     6\t  /** Display name of the token entry. */\n     7\t  owner: string;\n     8\t  /**\n     9\t   * Stable identity of the caller, stored on every session and compared on every call. For a static token it is\n    10\t   * `static:<owner>`; an OIDC verifier returns the token's `iss` + `sub` here.\n    11\t   */\n    12\t  subject: string;\n    13\t}\n    14\t\n    15\t/**\n    16\t * The single seam for authentication. Ingest and the orchestrator call this and nothing else, so an OIDC\n    17\t * verifier replaces `tokenAuthenticator` without touching a route. Resolves to undefined for \"not authenticated\".\n    18\t */\n    19\texport type Authenticator = (headers: IncomingHttpHeaders) => Promise<Principal | undefined>;\n    20\t\n    21\tconst OWNER = /^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,62}$/;\n    22\tconst MIN_TOKEN_LENGTH = 16;\n    23\t\n    24\tconst digest = (value: string): Buffer => createHash(\"sha256\").update(value).digest();\n    25\t\n    26\t/**\n    27\t * Static bearer tokens from a Kubernetes Secret, one `owner:token` entry per line (or comma). Every\n    28\t * candidate is compared in constant time, so the answer does not depend on which entry matched.\n    29\t * Error messages never contain a token.\n    30\t */\n    31\texport function tokenAuthenticator(spec: string): Authenticator {\n    32\t  const entries = spec\n    33\t    .split(/[\\n,]/)\n    34\t    .map((line) => line.trim())\n    35\t    .filter((line) => line !== \"\")\n    36\t    .map((line, index) => {\n    37\t      const at = line.indexOf(\":\");\n    38\t      const owner = at < 0 ? \"\" : line.slice(0, at);\n    39\t      const token = at < 0 ? \"\" : line.slice(at + 1);\n    40\t      if (!OWNER.test(owner) || token.length < MIN_TOKEN_LENGTH) {\n    41\t        throw new Error(\n    42\t          `API token entry ${String(index + 1)} must be owner:token (token at least ${String(MIN_TOKEN_LENGTH)} characters)`,\n    43\t        );\n    44\t      }\n    45\t      return { owner, hash: digest(token) };\n    46\t    });\n    47\t  if (entries.length === 0) throw new Error(\"no API tokens configured\");\n    48\t\n    49\t  return (headers) => {\n    50\t    const header = headers.authorization;\n    51\t    const match = typeof header === \"string\" ? /^Bearer +(\\S+)$/i.exec(header) : null;\n    52\t    const presented = digest(match?.[1] ?? \"\");\n    53\t    let found: string | undefined;\n    54\t    for (const entry of entries) {\n    55\t      if (timingSafeEqual(entry.hash, presented) && match !== null) found = entry.owner;\n    56\t    }\n    57\t    return Promise.resolve(\n    58\t      found === undefined ? undefined : { owner: found, subject: `static:${found}` },\n    59\t    );\n    60\t  };\n    61\t}\n=====packages/session-core/src/http.ts\n     1\timport type { IncomingMessage, ServerResponse } from \"node:http\";\n     2\t\n     3\texport function sendJson(\n     4\t  res: ServerResponse,\n     5\t  status: number,\n     6\t  body: unknown,\n     7\t  headers: Record<string, string> = {},\n     8\t): void {\n     9\t  res.writeHead(status, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\", ...headers });\n    10\t  res.end(JSON.stringify(body));\n    11\t}\n    12\t\n    13\texport class BodyError extends Error {}\n    14\t\n    15\t/** Reads a JSON object body, at most `limit` bytes. Throws BodyError for anything a client got wrong. */\n    16\texport async function readJsonObject(\n    17\t  req: IncomingMessage,\n    18\t  limit = 128 * 1024,\n    19\t): Promise<Record<string, unknown>> {\n    20\t  const chunks: Buffer[] = [];\n    21\t  let size = 0;\n    22\t  for await (const chunk of req) {\n    23\t    const buffer = chunk as Buffer;\n    24\t    size += buffer.length;\n    25\t    if (size > limit) throw new BodyError(\"body too large\");\n    26\t    chunks.push(buffer);\n    27\t  }\n    28\t  const text = Buffer.concat(chunks).toString(\"utf8\");\n    29\t  if (text.trim() === \"\") return {};\n    30\t  let parsed: unknown;\n    31\t  try {\n    32\t    parsed = JSON.parse(text);\n    33\t  } catch {\n    34\t    throw new BodyError(\"body is not valid JSON\");\n    35\t  }\n    36\t  if (typeof parsed !== \"object\" || parsed === null || Array.isArray(parsed)) {\n    37\t    throw new BodyError(\"body must be a JSON object\");\n    38\t  }\n    39\t  return parsed as Record<string, unknown>;\n    40\t}\n    41\t\n    42\texport const UUID = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/;\n    43\t\n    44\texport function errorMessage(error: unknown): string {\n    45\t  return error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n    46\t}\n=====packages/session-core/src/store.ts\n     1\timport { randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\n     2\timport type pg from \"pg\";\n     3\timport { THINKING_LEVELS } from \"./models.js\";\n     4\timport type { ModelChoice } from \"./models.js\";\n     5\timport type { RepoSpec } from \"./repo.js\";\n     6\t\n     7\t/** `failed` is terminal: the model credentials were rejected or the turn budget is used up. Only DELETE is accepted. */\n     8\texport type SessionStatus = \"active\" | \"deleting\" | \"deleted\" | \"failed\";\n     9\texport type EventKind = \"message\" | \"steer\" | \"cancel\" | \"delete\";\n    10\texport type EventStatus = \"pending\" | \"submitted\" | \"failed\";\n    11\t\n    12\texport interface SessionRow {\n    13\t  id: string;\n    14\t  owner: string;\n    15\t  /** Subject of the creating principal; the owner check compares this, not `owner`. */\n    16\t  ownerSubject: string | null;\n    17\t  status: SessionStatus;\n    18\t  /** Pi Durable conversation id; null until the orchestrator has created it. */\n    19\t  conversationId: number | null;\n    20\t  /** The model chosen at creation; null for sessions that predate migration 002 (they run the default). */\n    21\t  model: ModelChoice | null;\n    22\t  /** Why the session is `failed`; null otherwise. */\n    23\t  failure: string | null;\n    24\t  /** The repository workspace asked for at creation; null for a plain session (no OneCLI objects exist). */\n    25\t  repo: RepoSpec | null;\n    26\t  /** OneCLI agent and secret ids of a repo session, once provisioned. Ids only, never values. */\n    27\t  onecli: { agentId: string; secretIds: string[] } | null;\n    28\t  /** When the clone and the workspace marker were first completed; null before. */\n    29\t  workspaceReadyAt: Date | null;\n    30\t  createdAt: Date;\n    31\t  lastActivityAt: Date;\n    32\t}\n    33\t\n    34\texport interface InboxEvent {\n    35\t  /** bigint, so a string. Also the Pi Durable `requestId` of the submission. */\n    36\t  id: string;\n    37\t  sessionId: string;\n    38\t  source: string;\n    39\t  sourceEventId: string;\n    40\t  kind: EventKind;\n    41\t  payload: { text?: string; [key: string]: unknown };\n    42\t  status: EventStatus;\n    43\t  attempts: number;\n    44\t  createdAt: Date;\n    45\t  submittedAt: Date | null;\n    46\t  error: string | null;\n    47\t}\n    48\t\n    49\tinterface SessionDbRow {\n    50\t  id: string;\n    51\t  owner: string;\n    52\t  owner_subject: string | null;\n    53\t  status: SessionStatus;\n    54\t  conversation_id: string | null;\n    55\t  model_provider: string | null;\n    56\t  model_id: string | null;\n    57\t  model_reasoning: string | null;\n    58\t  failure: string | null;\n    59\t  repo: string | null;\n    60\t  repo_branch: string | null;\n    61\t  onecli_agent_id: string | null;\n    62\t  onecli_secret_ids: string[] | null;\n    63\t  workspace_ready_at: Date | null;\n    64\t  created_at: Date;\n    65\t  last_activity_at: Date;\n    66\t}\n    67\t\n    68\texport interface EventDbRow {\n    69\t  id: string;\n    70\t  session_id: string;\n    71\t  source: string;\n    72\t  source_event_id: string;\n    73\t  kind: EventKind;\n    74\t  payload: InboxEvent[\"payload\"];\n    75\t  status: EventStatus;\n    76\t  attempts: number;\n    77\t  created_at: Date;\n    78\t  submitted_at: Date | null;\n    79\t  error: string | null;\n    80\t}\n    81\t\n    82\tconst toSession = (row: SessionDbRow): SessionRow => ({\n    83\t  id: row.id,\n    84\t  owner: row.owner,\n    85\t  ownerSubject: row.owner_subject,\n    86\t  status: row.status,\n    87\t  conversationId: row.conversation_id === null ? null : Number(row.conversation_id),\n    88\t  model:\n    89\t    row.model_provider === null || row.model_id === null\n    90\t      ? null\n    91\t      : {\n    92\t          provider: row.model_provider,\n    93\t          model: row.model_id,\n    94\t          ...reasoningOf(row.model_reasoning),\n    95\t        },\n    96\t  failure: row.failure,\n    97\t  repo:\n    98\t    row.repo === null\n    99\t      ? null\n   100\t      : { repo: row.repo, ...(row.repo_branch === null ? {} : { branch: row.repo_branch }) },\n   101\t  onecli:\n   102\t    row.onecli_agent_id === null\n   103\t      ? null\n   104\t      : { agentId: row.onecli_agent_id, secretIds: row.onecli_secret_ids ?? [] },\n   105\t  workspaceReadyAt: row.workspace_ready_at,\n   106\t  createdAt: row.created_at,\n   107\t  lastActivityAt: row.last_activity_at,\n   108\t});\n   109\t\n   110\tfunction reasoningOf(value: string | null): Pick<ModelChoice, \"reasoning\"> {\n   111\t  const level = THINKING_LEVELS.find((candidate) => candidate === value);\n   112\t  return level === undefined ? {} : { reasoning: level };\n   113\t}\n   114\t\n   115\texport const toEvent = (row: EventDbRow): InboxEvent => ({\n   116\t  id: row.id,\n   117\t  sessionId: row.session_id,\n   118\t  source: row.source,\n   119\t  sourceEventId: row.source_event_id,\n   120\t  kind: row.kind,\n   121\t  payload: row.payload,\n   122\t  status: row.status,\n   123\t  attempts: row.attempts,\n   124\t  createdAt: row.created_at,\n   125\t  submittedAt: row.submitted_at,\n   126\t  error: row.error,\n   127\t});\n   128\t\n   129\t/** Session ids are random UUIDs (v4), never sequential: an id cannot be guessed from another. */\n   130\texport async function createSession(\n   131\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   132\t  principal: { owner: string; subject: string },\n   133\t  model: ModelChoice,\n   134\t  repo?: RepoSpec,\n   135\t): Promise<string> {\n   136\t  const id = randomUUID();\n   137\t  await pool.query(\n   138\t    \"insert into inbox.sessions (id, owner, owner_subject, model_provider, model_id, model_reasoning, repo, repo_branch) values ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, $6, $7, $8)\",\n   139\t    [\n   140\t      id,\n   141\t      principal.owner,\n   142\t      principal.subject,\n   143\t      model.provider,\n   144\t      model.model,\n   145\t      model.reasoning ?? null,\n   146\t      repo?.repo ?? null,\n   147\t      repo?.branch ?? null,\n   148\t    ],\n   149\t  );\n   150\t  return id;\n   151\t}\n   152\t\n   153\t/** Moves an active session to the terminal `failed` state. False if it was not active (failed already, deleting, deleted). */\n   154\texport async function failSession(\n   155\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   156\t  sessionId: string,\n   157\t  failure: string,\n   158\t): Promise<boolean> {\n   159\t  const result = await db.query(\n   160\t    `update inbox.sessions set status = 'failed', failure = $2, last_activity_at = clock_timestamp()\n   161\t      where id = $1 and status = 'active'`,\n   162\t    [sessionId, failure.slice(0, 500)],\n   163\t  );\n   164\t  return (result.rowCount ?? 0) > 0;\n   165\t}\n   166\t\n   167\texport async function getSession(\n   168\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   169\t  id: string,\n   170\t): Promise<SessionRow | undefined> {\n   171\t  const { rows } = await db.query<SessionDbRow>(\"select * from inbox.sessions where id = $1\", [id]);\n   172\t  const row = rows[0];\n   173\t  return row === undefined ? undefined : toSession(row);\n   174\t}\n   175\t\n   176\texport type EnqueueResult =\n   177\t  | { outcome: \"accepted\"; eventId: string }\n   178\t  /** The same (source, source_event_id) was already stored: nothing new was written. */\n   179\t  | { outcome: \"duplicate\"; eventId: string }\n   180\t  /** The (source, source_event_id) belongs to another session. */\n   181\t  | { outcome: \"conflict\" };\n   182\t\n   183\t/**\n   184\t * Writes one event and returns. The unique index on (source, source_event_id) makes a repeated post a no-op that\n   185\t * returns the first event's id. The orchestrator is not involved: this works while it is down.\n   186\t */\n   187\texport async function enqueueEvent(\n   188\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   189\t  event: {\n   190\t    sessionId: string;\n   191\t    source: string;\n   192\t    sourceEventId: string;\n   193\t    kind: EventKind;\n   194\t    payload: InboxEvent[\"payload\"];\n   195\t  },\n   196\t): Promise<EnqueueResult> {\n   197\t  const inserted = await pool.query<{ id: string }>(\n   198\t    `insert into inbox.events (session_id, source, source_event_id, kind, payload)\n   199\t     values ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5)\n   200\t     on conflict (source, source_event_id) do nothing\n   201\t     returning id`,\n   202\t    [event.sessionId, event.source, event.sourceEventId, event.kind, JSON.stringify(event.payload)],\n   203\t  );\n   204\t  const fresh = inserted.rows[0];\n   205\t  if (fresh !== undefined) {\n   206\t    await pool.query(\n   207\t      \"update inbox.sessions set last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1\",\n   208\t      [event.sessionId],\n   209\t    );\n   210\t    return { outcome: \"accepted\", eventId: fresh.id };\n   211\t  }\n   212\t  const { rows } = await pool.query<{ id: string; session_id: string }>(\n   213\t    \"select id, session_id from inbox.events where source = $1 and source_event_id = $2\",\n   214\t    [event.source, event.sourceEventId],\n   215\t  );\n   216\t  const existing = rows[0];\n   217\t  if (existing === undefined || existing.session_id !== event.sessionId) {\n   218\t    return { outcome: \"conflict\" };\n   219\t  }\n   220\t  return { outcome: \"duplicate\", eventId: existing.id };\n   221\t}\n   222\t\n   223\t/** Marks an active session as being deleted, so no further events are accepted. Idempotent. */\n   224\texport async function requestDelete(pool: pg.Pool, sessionId: string): Promise<void> {\n   225\t  await pool.query(\n   226\t    \"update inbox.sessions set status = 'deleting', last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1 and status in ('active', 'failed')\",\n   227\t    [sessionId],\n   228\t  );\n   229\t}\n   230\t\n   231\texport interface SessionSummary {\n   232\t  status: SessionStatus;\n   233\t  lastActivityAt: Date;\n   234\t  events: Record<EventStatus, number>;\n   235\t}\n   236\t\n   237\texport async function summarize(pool: pg.Pool, session: SessionRow): Promise<SessionSummary> {\n   238\t  const { rows } = await pool.query<{ status: EventStatus; n: string }>(\n   239\t    \"select status, count(*) as n from inbox.events where session_id = $1 group by status\",\n   240\t    [session.id],\n   241\t  );\n   242\t  const events: Record<EventStatus, number> = { pending: 0, submitted: 0, failed: 0 };\n   243\t  for (const row of rows) events[row.status] = Number(row.n);\n   244\t  return { status: session.status, lastActivityAt: session.lastActivityAt, events };\n   245\t}\n   246\t\n   247\t/** Records the OneCLI objects of a repo session. Ids only: no token or secret value is ever stored here. */\n   248\texport async function setOneCliObjects(\n   249\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   250\t  sessionId: string,\n   251\t  agentId: string,\n   252\t  secretIds: readonly string[],\n   253\t): Promise<void> {\n   254\t  await db.query(\n   255\t    \"update inbox.sessions set onecli_agent_id = $2, onecli_secret_ids = $3 where id = $1\",\n   256\t    [sessionId, agentId, [...secretIds]],\n   257\t  );\n   258\t}\n   259\t\n   260\t/** Marks the repo workspace as cloned. Keeps the first time if called again. */\n   261\texport async function markWorkspaceReady(\n   262\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   263\t  sessionId: string,\n   264\t): Promise<void> {\n   265\t  await db.query(\n   266\t    \"update inbox.sessions set workspace_ready_at = coalesce(workspace_ready_at, clock_timestamp()) where id = $1\",\n   267\t    [sessionId],\n   268\t  );\n   269\t}\n   270\t\n   271\t/**\n   272\t * First step of session deletion: records what the session held, so a crash before the OneCLI objects and the claim\n   273\t * are gone still leaves the list of what to revoke. Safe to repeat; the first record stays.\n   274\t */\n   275\texport async function writeTombstone(\n   276\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   277\t  session: SessionRow,\n   278\t): Promise<void> {\n   279\t  await db.query(\n   280\t    `insert into inbox.tombstones (session_id, conversation_id, repo, onecli_agent_id, onecli_secret_ids)\n   281\t     values ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5)\n   282\t     on conflict (session_id) do nothing`,\n   283\t    [\n   284\t      session.id,\n   285\t      session.conversationId,\n   286\t      session.repo?.repo ?? null,\n   287\t      session.onecli?.agentId ?? null,\n   288\t      session.onecli === null ? null : [...session.onecli.secretIds],\n   289\t    ],\n   290\t  );\n   291\t}\n   292\t\n   293\texport async function completeTombstone(\n   294\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   295\t  sessionId: string,\n   296\t): Promise<void> {\n   297\t  await db.query(\n   298\t    \"update inbox.tombstones set completed_at = coalesce(completed_at, clock_timestamp()) where session_id = $1\",\n   299\t    [sessionId],\n   300\t  );\n   301\t}\n   302\t\n   303\t/**\n   304\t * Records that a command may be running (or was interrupted) in the sandbox of this conversation. Called when a\n   305\t * burst of commands starts; a process that dies mid-command never clears it, which is the signal to recycle the Pod.\n   306\t * A conversation without a session row (the test-only control sessions) updates nothing.\n   307\t */\n   308\texport async function setExecInFlight(\n   309\t  db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">,\n   310\t  conversationId: number,\n   311\t  inFlight: boolean,\n   312\t): Promise<void> {\n   313\t  await db.query(\n   314\t    \"update inbox.sessions set exec_in_flight_at = case when $2::boolean then clock_timestamp() else null end where conversation_id = $1\",\n   315\t    [conversationId, inFlight],\n   316\t  );\n   317\t}\n   318\t\n   319\t/** Conversations whose sandbox had a command in flight when the last orchestrator process stopped. */\n   320\texport async function conversationsWithExecInFlight(db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">): Promise<number[]> {\n   321\t  const { rows } = await db.query<{ conversation_id: string }>(\n   322\t    \"select conversation_id from inbox.sessions where exec_in_flight_at is not null and conversation_id is not null and status in ('active', 'failed', 'deleting')\",\n   323\t  );\n   324\t  return rows.map((row) => Number(row.conversation_id));\n   325\t}\n   326\t\n   327\t/** What the orphan sweep needs to know about every session: no owner, model or repo. */\n   328\texport interface SessionRef {\n   329\t  id: string;\n   330\t  status: SessionStatus;\n   331\t  conversationId: number | null;\n   332\t}\n   333\t\n   334\texport async function listSessionRefs(db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">): Promise<SessionRef[]> {\n   335\t  const { rows } = await db.query<{\n   336\t    id: string;\n   337\t    status: SessionStatus;\n   338\t    conversation_id: string | null;\n   339\t  }>(\"select id, status, conversation_id from inbox.sessions\");\n   340\t  return rows.map((row) => ({\n   341\t    id: row.id,\n   342\t    status: row.status,\n   343\t    conversationId: row.conversation_id === null ? null : Number(row.conversation_id),\n   344\t  }));\n   345\t}\n=====packages/session-core/src/repo.ts\n     1\t/** A repository workspace requested at session creation. `branch` absent: the repository's default branch. */\n     2\texport interface RepoSpec {\n     3\t  /** `owner/name` on github.com. */\n     4\t  repo: string;\n     5\t  branch?: string;\n     6\t}\n     7\t\n     8\t// GitHub owners are 1-39 characters of letters, digits and single hyphens; names are up to 100 characters of\n     9\t// letters, digits, `.`, `_` and `-`. The first pattern is the contract; the length caps and the checks below\n    10\t// close what a character class cannot (`..`, `.git`, a leading dash that git would read as an option).\n    11\tconst REPO = /^[A-Za-z0-9-]+\\/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$/;\n    12\tconst REF = /^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._/-]*$/;\n    13\t\n    14\t/** Returns an error message, or undefined when `repo` is acceptable. */\n    15\texport function repoError(repo: string): string | undefined {\n    16\t  if (repo.length > 140 || !REPO.test(repo)) return \"repo must look like owner/name\";\n    17\t  const [owner = \"\", name = \"\"] = repo.split(\"/\");\n    18\t  if (owner.length > 39 || owner.startsWith(\"-\") || owner.endsWith(\"-\")) {\n    19\t    return \"repo owner is not a valid GitHub account name\";\n    20\t  }\n    21\t  if (repo.includes(\"..\") || name === \".\" || name.startsWith(\"-\")) {\n    22\t    return \"repo must not contain '..' or start a name with '-'\";\n    23\t  }\n    24\t  if (name.length > 100 || name.toLowerCase().endsWith(\".git\")) {\n    25\t    return \"repo name must not end in .git\";\n    26\t  }\n    27\t  return undefined;\n    28\t}\n    29\t\n    30\t/** Returns an error message, or undefined when `branch` is acceptable as a git ref name to clone. */\n    31\texport function branchError(branch: string): string | undefined {\n    32\t  if (branch.length > 200 || !REF.test(branch)) return \"branch is not a valid ref name\";\n    33\t  if (\n    34\t    branch.includes(\"..\") ||\n    35\t    branch.includes(\"//\") ||\n    36\t    branch.endsWith(\"/\") ||\n    37\t    branch.endsWith(\".\") ||\n    38\t    branch.endsWith(\".lock\") ||\n    39\t    branch.includes(\"/.\")\n    40\t  ) {\n    41\t    return \"branch is not a valid ref name\";\n    42\t  }\n    43\t  return undefined;\n    44\t}\n    45\t\n    46\t/**\n    47\t * Validates the optional `{ repo, branch }` of `POST /sessions`. `undefined` means no repository was asked for;\n    48\t * a string is the 400 message. Only `owner/name` on github.com over https exists: no URL is accepted anywhere,\n    49\t * the orchestrator builds `https://github.com/<repo>.git` itself.\n    50\t */\n    51\texport function chooseRepo(body: Record<string, unknown>): RepoSpec | string | undefined {\n    52\t  const { repo, branch } = body;\n    53\t  if (repo === undefined) return branch === undefined ? undefined : \"branch needs a repo\";\n    54\t  if (typeof repo !== \"string\") return \"repo must be a string like owner/name\";\n    55\t  const bad = repoError(repo);\n    56\t  if (bad !== undefined) return bad;\n    57\t  if (branch === undefined) return { repo };\n    58\t  if (typeof branch !== \"string\") return \"branch must be a string\";\n    59\t  const badBranch = branchError(branch);\n    60\t  if (badBranch !== undefined) return badBranch;\n    61\t  return { repo, branch };\n    62\t}\n    63\t\n    64\t/** The https clone URL of a validated repo. Credentials never appear in it: the OneCLI gateway injects them. */\n    65\texport function cloneUrl(repo: string, base = \"https://github.com\"): string {\n    66\t  return `${base}/${repo}.git`;\n    67\t}\n=====packages/session-core/src/models.ts\n     1\t/** A model a session runs on: a Pi provider id and a model id within it. */\n     2\texport interface ModelChoice {\n     3\t  provider: string;\n     4\t  model: string;\n     5\t  /** Reasoning effort (Pi's `thinkingLevel`); unset leaves it to Pi's default, `off`. */\n     6\t  reasoning?: ThinkingLevel;\n     7\t}\n     8\t\n     9\texport const THINKING_LEVELS = [\"off\", \"minimal\", \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\", \"xhigh\"] as const;\n    10\texport type ThinkingLevel = (typeof THINKING_LEVELS)[number];\n    11\t\n    12\t/** `provider/model`. The model id may itself contain slashes (`openrouter/openai/gpt-4.1-nano`). */\n    13\texport function modelKey(choice: ModelChoice): string {\n    14\t  return `${choice.provider}/${choice.model}`;\n    15\t}\n    16\t\n    17\t/** Parses one `provider/model` pair. Throws for anything else, naming the entry. */\n    18\texport function parseModelKey(entry: string): ModelChoice {\n    19\t  const slash = entry.indexOf(\"/\");\n    20\t  const provider = entry.slice(0, slash);\n    21\t  const model = entry.slice(slash + 1);\n    22\t  if (slash <= 0 || model === \"\" || /\\s/.test(entry)) {\n    23\t    throw new Error(`model allowlist entry \"${entry}\" is not provider/model`);\n    24\t  }\n    25\t  return { provider, model };\n    26\t}\n    27\t\n    28\t/** `PI_MODEL_ALLOWLIST`: comma- or newline-separated `provider/model` pairs. */\n    29\texport function parseAllowlist(spec: string): ModelChoice[] {\n    30\t  return spec\n    31\t    .split(/[,\\n]/)\n    32\t    .map((entry) => entry.trim())\n    33\t    .filter((entry) => entry !== \"\")\n    34\t    .map(parseModelKey);\n    35\t}\n    36\t\n    37\texport const DEFAULT_MODEL: ModelChoice = { provider: \"scripted\", model: \"scripted-1\" };\n    38\texport const DEFAULT_ALLOWLIST = \"scripted/scripted-1,scripted/scripted-2\";\n    39\t\n    40\texport interface ModelPolicy {\n    41\t  default: ModelChoice;\n    42\t  /** The default is always allowed, so a session without a model field cannot be refused. */\n    43\t  allowed: readonly ModelChoice[];\n    44\t  /** `PI_MODEL_REASONING`, applied to every new session; unset for none. */\n    45\t  reasoning?: ThinkingLevel;\n    46\t}\n    47\t\n    48\texport function loadModelPolicy(env: Readonly<Record<string, string | undefined>>): ModelPolicy {\n    49\t  const reasoning = parseReasoning(env.PI_MODEL_REASONING);\n    50\t  const defaultChoice: ModelChoice = {\n    51\t    ...parseModelKey(\n    52\t      `${env.PI_MODEL_PROVIDER ?? DEFAULT_MODEL.provider}/${env.PI_MODEL_ID ?? DEFAULT_MODEL.model}`,\n    53\t    ),\n    54\t    ...(reasoning === undefined ? {} : { reasoning }),\n    55\t  };\n    56\t  const listed = parseAllowlist(env.PI_MODEL_ALLOWLIST ?? DEFAULT_ALLOWLIST);\n    57\t  const seen = new Set<string>();\n    58\t  const allowed = [defaultChoice, ...listed].filter((choice) => {\n    59\t    const key = modelKey(choice);\n    60\t    if (seen.has(key)) return false;\n    61\t    seen.add(key);\n    62\t    return true;\n    63\t  });\n    64\t  return { default: defaultChoice, allowed, ...(reasoning === undefined ? {} : { reasoning }) };\n    65\t}\n    66\t\n    67\tfunction parseReasoning(value: string | undefined): ThinkingLevel | undefined {\n    68\t  if (value === undefined || value === \"\") return undefined;\n    69\t  const level = THINKING_LEVELS.find((candidate) => candidate === value);\n    70\t  if (level === undefined) {\n    71\t    throw new Error(`PI_MODEL_REASONING must be one of ${THINKING_LEVELS.join(\", \")}`);\n    72\t  }\n    73\t  return level;\n    74\t}\n    75\t\n    76\t/**\n    77\t * The model for a new session: the default when the body names none, else the requested pair if the allowlist has\n    78\t * it. A string is the 400 message.\n    79\t */\n    80\texport function chooseModel(\n    81\t  policy: ModelPolicy,\n    82\t  body: Record<string, unknown>,\n    83\t): ModelChoice | string {\n    84\t  const { provider, model } = body;\n    85\t  if (provider === undefined && model === undefined) return policy.default;\n    86\t  if (\n    87\t    typeof provider !== \"string\" ||\n    88\t    typeof model !== \"string\" ||\n    89\t    provider === \"\" ||\n    90\t    model === \"\"\n    91\t  ) {\n    92\t    return \"provider and model must both be non-empty strings\";\n    93\t  }\n    94\t  const requested: ModelChoice = {\n    95\t    provider,\n    96\t    model,\n    97\t    ...(policy.reasoning === undefined ? {} : { reasoning: policy.reasoning }),\n    98\t  };\n    99\t  const key = modelKey(requested);\n   100\t  if (!policy.allowed.some((choice) => modelKey(choice) === key)) {\n   101\t    return `model ${key.slice(0, 200)} is not allowed`;\n   102\t  }\n   103\t  return requested;\n   104\t}\n=====packages/session-core/src/migrate.ts\n     1\timport { readdir, readFile } from \"node:fs/promises\";\n     2\timport type pg from \"pg\";\n     3\t\n     4\tconst MIGRATIONS = new URL(\"../migrations/\", import.meta.url);\n     5\t/** Serialises concurrent starters (several ingest replicas plus the orchestrator). */\n     6\tconst LOCK_KEY = \"pi-durable-k8s:inbox-migrate\";\n     7\t\n     8\t/** Applies the inbox schema: every `NNN_*.sql` in order, each idempotent. Safe to call from every process at every start. */\n     9\texport async function applyMigrations(pool: pg.Pool): Promise<void> {\n    10\t  const files = (await readdir(MIGRATIONS)).filter((name) => name.endsWith(\".sql\")).sort();\n    11\t  const scripts = await Promise.all(\n    12\t    files.map((name) => readFile(new URL(name, MIGRATIONS), \"utf8\")),\n    13\t  );\n    14\t  const client = await pool.connect();\n    15\t  try {\n    16\t    await client.query(\"begin\");\n    17\t    await client.query(\"select pg_advisory_xact_lock(hashtextextended($1, 0))\", [LOCK_KEY]);\n    18\t    for (const sql of scripts) await client.query(sql);\n    19\t    await client.query(\"commit\");\n    20\t  } catch (error) {\n    21\t    await client.query(\"rollback\").catch(() => undefined);\n    22\t    throw error;\n    23\t  } finally {\n    24\t    client.release();\n    25\t  }\n    26\t}\n=====packages/orchestrator/src/http.ts\n     1\timport { createServer } from \"node:http\";\n     2\timport type { IncomingMessage, Server, ServerResponse } from \"node:http\";\n     3\timport { errorMessage, getSession, sendJson, UUID } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n     4\timport type { Authenticator } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n     5\timport type pg from \"pg\";\n     6\timport type { Host } from \"./host.js\";\n     7\timport { log } from \"./log.js\";\n     8\timport { parseScript } from \"./model.js\";\n     9\timport type { SessionService } from \"./sessions.js\";\n    10\timport { serveStream } from \"./stream.js\";\n    11\t\n    12\t/** What /readyz reports: ready only once this process holds the storage lock and the Harness is open. */\n    13\texport interface Lifecycle {\n    14\t  state: \"waiting-for-lock\" | \"owner\";\n    15\t  instance: string;\n    16\t  host?: Host;\n    17\t  service?: SessionService;\n    18\t}\n    19\t\n    20\texport interface ServerDeps {\n    21\t  lifecycle: Lifecycle;\n    22\t  authenticate: Authenticator;\n    23\t  /** For the owner check on the stream. Independent of the Pi Durable storage connection. */\n    24\t  pool: pg.Pool;\n    25\t  /** Mounts the test-only /control surface (PI_ORCH_CONTROL=1). */\n    26\t  control: boolean;\n    27\t}\n    28\t\n    29\tasync function readBody(req: IncomingMessage): Promise<string> {\n    30\t  const chunks: Buffer[] = [];\n    31\t  let size = 0;\n    32\t  for await (const chunk of req) {\n    33\t    const buffer = chunk as Buffer;\n    34\t    size += buffer.length;\n    35\t    if (size > 64 * 1024) throw new Error(\"body too large\");\n    36\t    chunks.push(buffer);\n    37\t  }\n    38\t  return Buffer.concat(chunks).toString(\"utf8\");\n    39\t}\n    40\t\n    41\t/**\n    42\t * The orchestrator's HTTP surface.\n    43\t *   GET /healthz                  liveness: 200 while the process runs\n    44\t *   GET /readyz                   200 once this process owns the schema and serves, else 503\n    45\t *   GET /sessions/{id}/stream     SSE; bearer token + owner check, the same Authenticator as ingest\n    46\t *   /control/...                  test-only (PI_ORCH_CONTROL=1): the Phase 3 scripted-session surface, same auth\n    47\t */\n    48\texport function createOrchestratorServer(deps: ServerDeps): Server {\n    49\t  const server = createServer((req, res) => {\n    50\t    void handle(req, res, deps).catch((error: unknown) => {\n    51\t      log(\"http-error\", { message: errorMessage(error) });\n    52\t      if (!res.headersSent) sendJson(res, 500, { error: \"internal error\" });\n    53\t      else res.destroy();\n    54\t    });\n    55\t  });\n    56\t  server.requestTimeout = 0;\n    57\t  return server;\n    58\t}\n    59\t\n    60\tasync function handle(req: IncomingMessage, res: ServerResponse, deps: ServerDeps): Promise<void> {\n    61\t  const { lifecycle } = deps;\n    62\t  const url = new URL(req.url ?? \"/\", \"http://localhost\");\n    63\t  const parts = url.pathname.split(\"/\").filter(Boolean);\n    64\t  const method = req.method ?? \"GET\";\n    65\t\n    66\t  if (method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/healthz\") {\n    67\t    sendJson(res, 200, { status: \"ok\", state: lifecycle.state, instance: lifecycle.instance });\n    68\t    return;\n    69\t  }\n    70\t  if (method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/readyz\") {\n    71\t    const ready = lifecycle.host !== undefined && lifecycle.service !== undefined;\n    72\t    sendJson(res, ready ? 200 : 503, { state: lifecycle.state, instance: lifecycle.instance });\n    73\t    return;\n    74\t  }\n    75\t\n    76\t  const principal = await deps.authenticate(req.headers);\n    77\t  if (principal === undefined) {\n    78\t    sendJson(res, 401, { error: \"unauthorized\" }, { \"www-authenticate\": \"Bearer\" });\n    79\t    return;\n    80\t  }\n    81\t\n    82\t  const { host, service } = lifecycle;\n    83\t  if (host === undefined || service === undefined) {\n    84\t    // Not the owner yet (starting, or waiting for the lock). Clients retry; ingest keeps accepting events.\n    85\t    sendJson(res, 503, { error: lifecycle.state }, { \"retry-after\": \"2\" });\n    86\t    return;\n    87\t  }\n    88\t\n    89\t  if (method === \"GET\" && parts.length === 3 && parts[0] === \"sessions\" && parts[2] === \"stream\") {\n    90\t    const id = parts[1] ?? \"\";\n    91\t    const session = UUID.test(id) ? await getSession(deps.pool, id) : undefined;\n    92\t    if (session?.ownerSubject !== principal.subject) {\n    93\t      sendJson(res, 404, { error: \"session not found\" });\n    94\t      return;\n    95\t    }\n    96\t    if (session.status === \"deleted\") {\n    97\t      sendJson(res, 410, { error: \"session deleted\" });\n    98\t      return;\n    99\t    }\n   100\t    const conversationId = await service.ensureConversation(session);\n   101\t    await serveStream(req, res, host, service.streams, session.id, conversationId);\n   102\t    return;\n   103\t  }\n   104\t\n   105\t  if (deps.control && parts[0] === \"control\") {\n   106\t    await handleControl(req, res, host, method, parts.slice(1));\n   107\t    return;\n   108\t  }\n   109\t  sendJson(res, 404, { error: \"not found\" });\n   110\t}\n   111\t\n   112\t/**\n   113\t * Test-only. Scripted sessions created straight on the Harness, not through the inbox, with the sandbox claim\n   114\t * created eagerly. Kept only so the Phase 3 failure tests keep running unchanged in substance.\n   115\t *   POST /control/sessions            body = script JSON\n   116\t *   POST /control/sessions/:id/inputs body = script JSON\n   117\t *   GET  /control/sessions/:id        status and tool results\n   118\t */\n   119\tasync function handleControl(\n   120\t  req: IncomingMessage,\n   121\t  res: ServerResponse,\n   122\t  host: Host,\n   123\t  method: string,\n   124\t  parts: string[],\n   125\t): Promise<void> {\n   126\t  if (parts[0] !== \"sessions\") {\n   127\t    sendJson(res, 404, { error: \"not found\" });\n   128\t    return;\n   129\t  }\n   130\t  if (method === \"POST\" && parts.length === 1) {\n   131\t    let script;\n   132\t    try {\n   133\t      script = parseScript(await readBody(req));\n   134\t    } catch (error) {\n   135\t      sendJson(res, 400, { error: errorMessage(error) });\n   136\t      return;\n   137\t    }\n   138\t    sendJson(res, 201, await host.startSession(script));\n   139\t    return;\n   140\t  }\n   141\t  const id = Number(parts[1]);\n   142\t  if (method === \"POST\" && parts[2] === \"inputs\") {\n   143\t    let script;\n   144\t    try {\n   145\t      script = parseScript(await readBody(req));\n   146\t    } catch (error) {\n   147\t      sendJson(res, 400, { error: errorMessage(error) });\n   148\t      return;\n   149\t    }\n   150\t    const known = Number.isInteger(id) && (await host.sendInput(id, script));\n   151\t    sendJson(res, known ? 202 : 404, known ? { id } : { error: \"unknown session\" });\n   152\t    return;\n   153\t  }\n   154\t  if (method === \"GET\" && parts.length === 2 && Number.isInteger(id)) {\n   155\t    const status = await host.status(id);\n   156\t    sendJson(res, status === undefined ? 404 : 200, status ?? { error: \"unknown session\" });\n   157\t    return;\n   158\t  }\n   159\t  sendJson(res, 404, { error: \"not found\" });\n   160\t}\n=====packages/session-core/migrations/001_inbox.sql\n     1\t-- Inbox schema of the session API. Own schema, separate from the Pi Durable storage schema (`durable`).\n     2\t-- Idempotent: ingest and the orchestrator both apply it at start (under an advisory lock, see migrate.ts).\n     3\t\n     4\tcreate schema if not exists inbox;\n     5\t\n     6\t-- One row per API session. `conversation_id` is the Pi Durable conversation, set by the orchestrator when it\n     7\t-- creates the conversation (lazily, on the first event or stream). One session = one conversation = one\n     8\t-- SandboxClaim (`pi-conv-<conversation_id>`) = one PVC.\n     9\tcreate table if not exists inbox.sessions (\n    10\t  id               uuid primary key,\n    11\t  owner            text not null,\n    12\t  status           text not null default 'active' check (status in ('active', 'deleting', 'deleted')),\n    13\t  conversation_id  bigint,\n    14\t  created_at       timestamptz not null default clock_timestamp(),\n    15\t  last_activity_at timestamptz not null default clock_timestamp()\n    16\t);\n    17\t\n    18\t-- The owner check compares the caller's subject (static tokens: `static:<owner>`, OIDC: iss + sub), not the name.\n    19\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists owner_subject text;\n    20\t\n    21\tcreate table if not exists inbox.events (\n    22\t  id              bigint generated always as identity primary key,\n    23\t  session_id      uuid not null references inbox.sessions (id),\n    24\t  source          text not null,\n    25\t  source_event_id text not null,\n    26\t  kind            text not null check (kind in ('message', 'steer', 'cancel', 'delete')),\n    27\t  payload         jsonb not null default '{}',\n    28\t  status          text not null default 'pending' check (status in ('pending', 'submitted', 'failed')),\n    29\t  attempts        integer not null default 0,\n    30\t  created_at      timestamptz not null default clock_timestamp(),\n    31\t  submitted_at    timestamptz,\n    32\t  error           text\n    33\t);\n    34\t\n    35\t-- Deduplication: the same (source, source_event_id) is one event, however often it is posted.\n    36\tcreate unique index if not exists events_source_dedup on inbox.events (source, source_event_id);\n    37\t-- The orchestrator's claim query: pending rows of one session in arrival order.\n    38\tcreate index if not exists events_pending_by_session\n    39\t  on inbox.events (session_id, created_at, id) where status = 'pending';\n    40\tcreate index if not exists events_pending_any on inbox.events (created_at, id) where status = 'pending';\n    41\t\n    42\t-- Wakes the orchestrator's LISTEN so a new event does not wait for the poll interval.\n    43\tcreate or replace function inbox.notify_event() returns trigger language plpgsql as $$\n    44\tbegin\n    45\t  perform pg_notify('inbox_events', new.session_id::text);\n    46\t  return new;\n    47\tend $$;\n    48\t\n    49\tdrop trigger if exists events_notify on inbox.events;\n    50\tcreate trigger events_notify after insert on inbox.events\n    51\t  for each row execute function inbox.notify_event();\n=====packages/session-core/migrations/002_models.sql\n     1\t-- Phase 4b: each session records the model it was created with, and a terminal `failed` state.\n     2\t-- Idempotent, like 001.\n     3\t\n     4\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists model_provider text;\n     5\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists model_id text;\n     6\t-- Why the session is `failed` (model credentials rejected, turn budget used up). Null otherwise.\n     7\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists failure text;\n     8\t\n     9\t-- `failed` is terminal: no further events are accepted, only DELETE. Replace the inline check from 001, once.\n    10\tdo $$\n    11\tbegin\n    12\t  if exists (\n    13\t    select 1 from pg_constraint\n    14\t     where conrelid = 'inbox.sessions'::regclass\n    15\t       and conname = 'sessions_status_check'\n    16\t       and pg_get_constraintdef(oid) not like '%failed%'\n    17\t  ) then\n    18\t    alter table inbox.sessions drop constraint sessions_status_check;\n    19\t    alter table inbox.sessions add constraint sessions_status_check\n    20\t      check (status in ('active', 'deleting', 'deleted', 'failed'));\n    21\t  end if;\n    22\tend $$;\n=====packages/session-core/migrations/003_reasoning.sql\n     1\t-- Reasoning effort (Pi's thinkingLevel) a session was created with. Null: none stored, Pi's default (off) applies.\n     2\t-- Idempotent, like 001 and 002.\n     3\t\n     4\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists model_reasoning text;\n=====packages/session-core/migrations/004_repo.sql\n     1\t-- Phase 4c: an optional repository workspace per session, and the OneCLI objects that serve it.\n     2\t-- Idempotent, like 001 to 003.\n     3\t\n     4\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists repo text;          -- `owner/name`, null: no repository\n     5\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists repo_branch text;   -- null: the repository's default branch\n     6\t-- The session's OneCLI agent and per-session secrets (ids, never values). Null until provisioned.\n     7\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists onecli_agent_id text;\n     8\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists onecli_secret_ids text[];\n     9\t-- Set once the clone is done and the workspace marker exists. A later missing marker means the workspace was\n    10\t-- lost, which is reported instead of silently cloned again.\n    11\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists workspace_ready_at timestamptz;\n    12\t\n    13\t-- Written first when a session is deleted, before any OneCLI object or claim goes away, so a crash mid-delete\n    14\t-- leaves a record of what still has to be revoked. Never deleted: it is the audit trail of what a session held.\n    15\tcreate table if not exists inbox.tombstones (\n    16\t  session_id        uuid primary key,\n    17\t  conversation_id   bigint,\n    18\t  repo              text,\n    19\t  onecli_agent_id   text,\n    20\t  onecli_secret_ids text[],\n    21\t  created_at        timestamptz not null default clock_timestamp(),\n    22\t  completed_at      timestamptz\n    23\t);\n=====packages/session-core/migrations/005_exec_in_flight.sql\n     1\t-- Sandbox lifecycle: which sessions had a command running in their sandbox. Set when the first command of a burst\n     2\t-- starts, cleared when the last one ended without being interrupted. A row that is still set at orchestrator start\n     3\t-- means the previous process died mid-command, so the sandbox Pod may hold `setsid` children that survived the\n     4\t-- kill: the orchestrator recycles that Pod (never the claim or the PVC). Idempotent, like 001 to 004.\n     5\t\n     6\talter table inbox.sessions add column if not exists exec_in_flight_at timestamptz;\n<harness>\n[info] Full output: /tmp/tmp-iKPDNo/pi-output-2ae401e9-fe27-46c1-b8a1-5afd8615411b.log\n[warn] Output truncated to its end: 147 lines, 5496 bytes dropped\n</harness>","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 9555 {"id":9555,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]","calls":["bash({\"command\":\"cd /workspace/repo && nl -ba packages/ingest/src/server.ts | sed -n '1,240p'; nl -ba packages/orchestrator/src/inbox.ts | sed -n '1,260p'; nl -ba packages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts | sed -n '1,200p'\",\"timeout\":10000})"]}]}
ENTRY 9563 {"id":9563,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"     1\timport { request as httpRequest, createServer } from \"node:http\";\n     2\timport type { IncomingMessage, Server, ServerResponse } from \"node:http\";\n     3\timport { URL } from \"node:url\";\n     4\timport type pg from \"pg\";\n     5\timport {\n     6\t  BodyError,\n     7\t  chooseModel,\n     8\t  chooseRepo,\n     9\t  createSession,\n    10\t  enqueueEvent,\n    11\t  errorMessage,\n    12\t  getSession,\n    13\t  readJsonObject,\n    14\t  requestDelete,\n    15\t  sendJson,\n    16\t  summarize,\n    17\t  UUID,\n    18\t} from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n    19\timport type {\n    20\t  Authenticator,\n    21\t  ModelChoice,\n    22\t  ModelPolicy,\n    23\t  Principal,\n    24\t  SessionRow,\n    25\t} from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n    26\timport { parseEventBody } from \"./events.js\";\n    27\timport { log } from \"./log.js\";\n    28\t\n    29\texport interface IngestDeps {\n    30\t  pool: pg.Pool;\n    31\t  authenticate: Authenticator;\n    32\t  orchestratorUrl: string;\n    33\t  models: ModelPolicy;\n    34\t}\n    35\t\n    36\texport function createIngestServer(deps: IngestDeps): Server {\n    37\t  return createServer((req, res) => {\n    38\t    void handle(req, res, deps).catch((error: unknown) => {\n    39\t      log(\"http-error\", { message: errorMessage(error) });\n    40\t      if (!res.headersSent) sendJson(res, 500, { error: \"internal error\" });\n    41\t      else res.destroy();\n    42\t    });\n    43\t  });\n    44\t}\n    45\t\n    46\tasync function handle(req: IncomingMessage, res: ServerResponse, deps: IngestDeps): Promise<void> {\n    47\t  const url = new URL(req.url ?? \"/\", \"http://localhost\");\n    48\t  const parts = url.pathname.split(\"/\").filter(Boolean);\n    49\t  const method = req.method ?? \"GET\";\n    50\t\n    51\t  if (method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/healthz\") {\n    52\t    sendJson(res, 200, { status: \"ok\" });\n    53\t    return;\n    54\t  }\n    55\t  if (method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/readyz\") {\n    56\t    // Ready means \"can accept events\": the database answers. The orchestrator is deliberately not checked.\n    57\t    try {\n    58\t      await deps.pool.query(\"select 1\");\n    59\t      sendJson(res, 200, { status: \"ready\" });\n    60\t    } catch {\n    61\t      sendJson(res, 503, { status: \"database unavailable\" });\n    62\t    }\n    63\t    return;\n    64\t  }\n    65\t\n    66\t  // Every route below is behind this one check.\n    67\t  const principal = await deps.authenticate(req.headers);\n    68\t  if (principal === undefined) {\n    69\t    sendJson(res, 401, { error: \"unauthorized\" }, { \"www-authenticate\": \"Bearer\" });\n    70\t    return;\n    71\t  }\n    72\t\n    73\t  if (method === \"POST\" && url.pathname === \"/sessions\") {\n    74\t    await postSession(req, res, deps, principal);\n    75\t    return;\n    76\t  }\n    77\t  if (parts[0] !== \"sessions\" || parts[1] === undefined) {\n    78\t    sendJson(res, 404, { error: \"not found\" });\n    79\t    return;\n    80\t  }\n    81\t  const session = await ownedSession(deps.pool, parts[1], principal);\n    82\t  if (session === undefined) {\n    83\t    // Unknown id and someone else's id look the same: the API does not reveal that a session exists.\n    84\t    sendJson(res, 404, { error: \"session not found\" });\n    85\t    return;\n    86\t  }\n    87\t\n    88\t  if (parts.length === 2 && method === \"GET\") {\n    89\t    const summary = await summarize(deps.pool, session);\n    90\t    sendJson(res, 200, {\n    91\t      sessionId: session.id,\n    92\t      status: summary.status,\n    93\t      model: modelOf(session, deps.models),\n    94\t      ...(session.repo === null ? {} : { repo: session.repo }),\n    95\t      ...(session.failure === null ? {} : { failure: session.failure }),\n    96\t      createdAt: session.createdAt.toISOString(),\n    97\t      lastActivityAt: summary.lastActivityAt.toISOString(),\n    98\t      events: summary.events,\n    99\t    });\n   100\t    return;\n   101\t  }\n   102\t  if (parts.length === 2 && method === \"DELETE\") {\n   103\t    await queueDelete(deps.pool, session, principal, res);\n   104\t    return;\n   105\t  }\n   106\t  if (parts.length === 3 && parts[2] === \"events\" && method === \"POST\") {\n   107\t    await postEvent(req, res, deps.pool, session, principal);\n   108\t    return;\n   109\t  }\n   110\t  if (parts.length === 3 && parts[2] === \"stream\" && method === \"GET\") {\n   111\t    if (session.status === \"deleted\") {\n   112\t      sendJson(res, 410, { error: \"session deleted\" });\n   113\t      return;\n   114\t    }\n   115\t    proxyStream(req, res, deps.orchestratorUrl, session.id);\n   116\t    return;\n   117\t  }\n   118\t  sendJson(res, 404, { error: \"not found\" });\n   119\t}\n   120\t\n   121\t/** Sessions that predate migration 002 have no stored model: they run the default. */\n   122\tfunction modelOf(session: SessionRow, policy: ModelPolicy): ModelChoice {\n   123\t  return session.model ?? policy.default;\n   124\t}\n   125\t\n   126\tasync function postSession(\n   127\t  req: IncomingMessage,\n   128\t  res: ServerResponse,\n   129\t  deps: IngestDeps,\n   130\t  principal: Principal,\n   131\t): Promise<void> {\n   132\t  let body: Record<string, unknown>;\n   133\t  try {\n   134\t    body = await readJsonObject(req);\n   135\t  } catch (error) {\n   136\t    if (error instanceof BodyError) {\n   137\t      sendJson(res, 400, { error: error.message });\n   138\t      return;\n   139\t    }\n   140\t    throw error;\n   141\t  }\n   142\t  const model = chooseModel(deps.models, body);\n   143\t  if (typeof model === \"string\") {\n   144\t    sendJson(res, 400, { error: model });\n   145\t    return;\n   146\t  }\n   147\t  const repo = chooseRepo(body);\n   148\t  if (typeof repo === \"string\") {\n   149\t    sendJson(res, 400, { error: repo });\n   150\t    return;\n   151\t  }\n   152\t  const sessionId = await createSession(deps.pool, principal, model, repo);\n   153\t  sendJson(res, 201, {\n   154\t    sessionId,\n   155\t    provider: model.provider,\n   156\t    model: model.model,\n   157\t    ...(model.reasoning === undefined ? {} : { reasoning: model.reasoning }),\n   158\t    ...(repo === undefined\n   159\t      ? {}\n   160\t      : { repo: repo.repo, ...(repo.branch === undefined ? {} : { branch: repo.branch }) }),\n   161\t  });\n   162\t}\n   163\t\n   164\tasync function ownedSession(\n   165\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   166\t  id: string,\n   167\t  principal: Principal,\n   168\t): Promise<SessionRow | undefined> {\n   169\t  if (!UUID.test(id)) return undefined;\n   170\t  const session = await getSession(pool, id);\n   171\t  return session?.ownerSubject === principal.subject ? session : undefined;\n   172\t}\n   173\t\n   174\tasync function postEvent(\n   175\t  req: IncomingMessage,\n   176\t  res: ServerResponse,\n   177\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   178\t  session: SessionRow,\n   179\t  principal: Principal,\n   180\t): Promise<void> {\n   181\t  let parsed;\n   182\t  try {\n   183\t    parsed = parseEventBody(await readJsonObject(req));\n   184\t  } catch (error) {\n   185\t    if (error instanceof BodyError) {\n   186\t      sendJson(res, 400, { error: error.message });\n   187\t      return;\n   188\t    }\n   189\t    throw error;\n   190\t  }\n   191\t  if (typeof parsed === \"string\") {\n   192\t    sendJson(res, 400, { error: parsed });\n   193\t    return;\n   194\t  }\n   195\t  if (session.status !== \"active\") {\n   196\t    sendJson(res, session.status === \"deleted\" ? 410 : 409, {\n   197\t      error: `session is ${session.status}`,\n   198\t    });\n   199\t    return;\n   200\t  }\n   201\t  const result = await enqueueEvent(pool, {\n   202\t    sessionId: session.id,\n   203\t    source: `api:${principal.owner}`,\n   204\t    sourceEventId: parsed.sourceEventId,\n   205\t    kind: parsed.kind,\n   206\t    payload: parsed.payload,\n   207\t  });\n   208\t  if (result.outcome === \"conflict\") {\n   209\t    sendJson(res, 409, { error: \"sourceEventId was already used for another session\" });\n   210\t    return;\n   211\t  }\n   212\t  // 202 either way: a repeated post is accepted and names the first event.\n   213\t  sendJson(res, 202, { eventId: result.eventId, duplicate: result.outcome === \"duplicate\" });\n   214\t}\n   215\t\n   216\tasync function queueDelete(\n   217\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   218\t  session: SessionRow,\n   219\t  principal: Principal,\n   220\t  res: ServerResponse,\n   221\t): Promise<void> {\n   222\t  if (session.status === \"deleted\") {\n   223\t    sendJson(res, 202, { sessionId: session.id, status: \"deleted\" });\n   224\t    return;\n   225\t  }\n   226\t  // The delete is an inbox row like any other, so it runs after the events accepted before it.\n   227\t  const result = await enqueueEvent(pool, {\n   228\t    sessionId: session.id,\n   229\t    source: `api:${principal.owner}`,\n   230\t    sourceEventId: `delete:${session.id}`,\n   231\t    kind: \"delete\",\n   232\t    payload: {},\n   233\t  });\n   234\t  await requestDelete(pool, session.id);\n   235\t  const eventId = result.outcome === \"conflict\" ? undefined : result.eventId;\n   236\t  sendJson(res, 202, { sessionId: session.id, status: \"deleting\", eventId });\n   237\t}\n   238\t\n   239\t/**\n   240\t * Pipes the orchestrator's SSE stream to the client. The orchestrator authenticates the same token again.\n     1\timport type pg from \"pg\";\n     2\timport { errorMessage, getSession, toEvent } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n     3\timport type { EventDbRow, InboxEvent, SessionRow } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n     4\timport { log } from \"./log.js\";\n     5\timport { PermanentError } from \"./sessions.js\";\n     6\t\n     7\tconst POLL_MS = 1_000;\n     8\tconst BATCH = 20;\n     9\tconst MAX_PARALLEL_SESSIONS = 8;\n    10\tconst MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5;\n    11\t\n    12\texport type ApplyEvent = (event: InboxEvent, session: SessionRow) => Promise<void>;\n    13\t\n    14\t/**\n    15\t * The orchestrator's side of the inbox. It claims `pending` rows, hands each to Pi Durable (the row id is the\n    16\t * `requestId`), and only then marks the row `submitted`. Pi Durable owns run recovery: a row that is\n    17\t * already `submitted` is never touched again, so a run that died is never re-run from here.\n    18\t *\n    19\t *  - Wake-up: LISTEN on `inbox_events` (sent by a trigger on insert) plus a short poll as the safety net.\n    20\t *  - Claim: one transaction per session batch, `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, oldest first. The row locks are held\n    21\t *    until the rows are marked, so a crash in between rolls the batch back to `pending`; the retry submits\n    22\t *    with the same `requestId` and Pi Durable returns the original submission.\n    23\t *  - Ordering: one drain per session at a time, rows in (created_at, id) order. A transient failure stops\n    24\t *    that session's batch so later rows cannot overtake it; other sessions are unaffected.\n    25\t *  - Batching: rows of a session are claimed up to 20 at a time and submitted one by one, in order. They are\n    26\t *    not merged into one input: each keeps its own requestId and therefore its own idempotent submission.\n    27\t */\n    28\texport class InboxLoop {\n    29\t  readonly #pool: pg.Pool;\n    30\t  readonly #apply: ApplyEvent;\n    31\t  readonly #inFlight = new Set<string>();\n    32\t  #listener: pg.PoolClient | undefined;\n    33\t  #timer: NodeJS.Timeout | undefined;\n    34\t  #ticking = false;\n    35\t  #again = false;\n    36\t  #stopped = false;\n    37\t\n    38\t  constructor(pool: pg.Pool, apply: ApplyEvent) {\n    39\t    this.#pool = pool;\n    40\t    this.#apply = apply;\n    41\t  }\n    42\t\n    43\t  start(): void {\n    44\t    void this.#listen();\n    45\t    this.#timer = setInterval(() => this.wake(), POLL_MS);\n    46\t    this.wake();\n    47\t  }\n    48\t\n    49\t  async stop(): Promise<void> {\n    50\t    this.#stopped = true;\n    51\t    if (this.#timer !== undefined) clearInterval(this.#timer);\n    52\t    this.#listener?.removeAllListeners();\n    53\t    this.#listener?.release(true);\n    54\t    // Let drains in flight finish their current row: they hold row locks and a transaction.\n    55\t    while (this.#inFlight.size > 0) await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n    56\t  }\n    57\t\n    58\t  wake(): void {\n    59\t    if (this.#stopped) return;\n    60\t    if (this.#ticking) {\n    61\t      this.#again = true;\n    62\t      return;\n    63\t    }\n    64\t    this.#ticking = true;\n    65\t    void this.#tick().finally(() => {\n    66\t      this.#ticking = false;\n    67\t      if (this.#again) {\n    68\t        this.#again = false;\n    69\t        this.wake();\n    70\t      }\n    71\t    });\n    72\t  }\n    73\t\n    74\t  async #listen(): Promise<void> {\n    75\t    while (!this.#stopped) {\n    76\t      try {\n    77\t        const client = await this.#pool.connect();\n    78\t        this.#listener = client;\n    79\t        await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {\n    80\t          client.on(\"notification\", () => this.wake());\n    81\t          client.on(\"error\", () => resolve());\n    82\t          client.on(\"end\", () => resolve());\n    83\t          client.query(\"listen inbox_events\").catch(() => resolve());\n    84\t        });\n    85\t        client.removeAllListeners();\n    86\t        client.release(true);\n    87\t      } catch (error) {\n    88\t        log(\"inbox-listen-failed\", { message: errorMessage(error) });\n    89\t      }\n    90\t      // The poll covers the gap until the listener is back.\n    91\t      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 2_000));\n    92\t    }\n    93\t  }\n    94\t\n    95\t  async #tick(): Promise<void> {\n    96\t    try {\n    97\t      const { rows } = await this.#pool.query<{ session_id: string }>(\n    98\t        \"select distinct session_id from inbox.events where status = 'pending' limit 100\",\n    99\t      );\n   100\t      for (const { session_id: sessionId } of rows) {\n   101\t        if (this.#inFlight.has(sessionId) || this.#inFlight.size >= MAX_PARALLEL_SESSIONS) continue;\n   102\t        this.#inFlight.add(sessionId);\n   103\t        void this.#drain(sessionId)\n   104\t          .then((progressed) => {\n   105\t            if (progressed) this.wake();\n   106\t          })\n   107\t          .catch((error: unknown) => {\n   108\t            log(\"inbox-drain-failed\", { session: sessionId, message: errorMessage(error) });\n   109\t          })\n   110\t          .finally(() => this.#inFlight.delete(sessionId));\n   111\t      }\n   112\t    } catch (error) {\n   113\t      log(\"inbox-poll-failed\", { message: errorMessage(error) });\n   114\t    }\n   115\t  }\n   116\t\n   117\t  /** Claims and applies batches for one session until none is pending. True if it made progress. */\n   118\t  async #drain(sessionId: string): Promise<boolean> {\n   119\t    let progressed = false;\n   120\t    while (!this.#stopped) {\n   121\t      const client = await this.#pool.connect();\n   122\t      let finished = true;\n   123\t      try {\n   124\t        await client.query(\"begin\");\n   125\t        const { rows } = await client.query<EventDbRow>(\n   126\t          `select * from inbox.events\n   127\t            where session_id = $1 and status = 'pending'\n   128\t            order by created_at, id\n   129\t            limit $2\n   130\t            for update skip locked`,\n   131\t          [sessionId, BATCH],\n   132\t        );\n   133\t        if (rows.length === 0) {\n   134\t          await client.query(\"commit\");\n   135\t          return progressed;\n   136\t        }\n   137\t        for (const row of rows) {\n   138\t          const event = toEvent(row);\n   139\t          const outcome = await this.#applyRow(client, event);\n   140\t          if (outcome === \"retry-later\") {\n   141\t            finished = false;\n   142\t            break;\n   143\t          }\n   144\t          progressed = true;\n   145\t        }\n   146\t        await client.query(\"commit\");\n   147\t      } catch (error) {\n   148\t        await client.query(\"rollback\").catch(() => undefined);\n   149\t        throw error;\n   150\t      } finally {\n   151\t        client.release();\n   152\t      }\n   153\t      if (!finished) return progressed;\n   154\t    }\n   155\t    return progressed;\n   156\t  }\n   157\t\n   158\t  async #applyRow(client: pg.PoolClient, event: InboxEvent): Promise<\"done\" | \"retry-later\"> {\n   159\t    const attempt = event.attempts + 1;\n   160\t    try {\n   161\t      const session = await getSession(client, event.sessionId);\n   162\t      if (session === undefined) throw new PermanentError(\"session does not exist\");\n   163\t      await this.#apply(event, session);\n   164\t      await client.query(\n   165\t        `update inbox.events\n   166\t            set status = 'submitted', submitted_at = clock_timestamp(), attempts = $2, error = null\n   167\t          where id = $1`,\n   168\t        [event.id, attempt],\n   169\t      );\n   170\t      await client.query(\n   171\t        \"update inbox.sessions set last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1\",\n   172\t        [event.sessionId],\n   173\t      );\n   174\t      log(\"event-submitted\", { eventId: event.id, session: event.sessionId, kind: event.kind });\n   175\t      return \"done\";\n   176\t    } catch (error) {\n   177\t      const message = errorMessage(error).slice(0, 500);\n   178\t      const permanent = error instanceof PermanentError || attempt >= MAX_ATTEMPTS;\n   179\t      await client.query(\n   180\t        \"update inbox.events set status = $2, attempts = $3, error = $4 where id = $1\",\n   181\t        [event.id, permanent ? \"failed\" : \"pending\", attempt, message],\n   182\t      );\n   183\t      log(\"event-failed\", {\n   184\t        eventId: event.id,\n   185\t        session: event.sessionId,\n   186\t        attempt,\n   187\t        permanent,\n   188\t        message,\n   189\t      });\n   190\t      return permanent ? \"done\" : \"retry-later\";\n   191\t    }\n   192\t  }\n   193\t}\n     1\timport { writeSync } from \"node:fs\";\n     2\timport type pg from \"pg\";\n     3\timport {\n     4\t  completeTombstone,\n     5\t  errorMessage,\n     6\t  failSession,\n     7\t  getSession,\n     8\t  writeTombstone,\n     9\t} from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n    10\timport type { InboxEvent, ModelChoice, SessionRow } from \"@pi-durable-k8s/session-core\";\n    11\timport { terminalFailure } from \"./failure.js\";\n    12\timport type { RunOutcome } from \"./failure.js\";\n    13\timport { GithubDeniedError } from \"./github-app.js\";\n    14\timport type { Host } from \"./host.js\";\n    15\timport { log } from \"./log.js\";\n    16\timport { RepoUnavailableError } from \"./repo-access.js\";\n    17\timport type { RepoAccess } from \"./repo-access.js\";\n    18\timport { WorkspaceLostError } from \"./workspace.js\";\n    19\timport { RunWatcher } from \"./watcher.js\";\n    20\timport type { Watched } from \"./watcher.js\";\n    21\t\n    22\t/** An event that can never succeed (deleted session, malformed payload): the row is marked failed, not retried. */\n    23\texport class PermanentError extends Error {}\n    24\t\n    25\t/** Open SSE streams by session, so deleting a session can end them. */\n    26\texport class StreamRegistry {\n    27\t  readonly #streams = new Map<string, Set<(reason: string) => void>>();\n    28\t\n    29\t  add(sessionId: string, close: (reason: string) => void): () => void {\n    30\t    let set = this.#streams.get(sessionId);\n    31\t    if (set === undefined) {\n    32\t      set = new Set();\n    33\t      this.#streams.set(sessionId, set);\n    34\t    }\n    35\t    set.add(close);\n    36\t    return () => {\n    37\t      set.delete(close);\n    38\t      if (set.size === 0) this.#streams.delete(sessionId);\n    39\t    };\n    40\t  }\n    41\t\n    42\t  closeSession(sessionId: string, reason: string): void {\n    43\t    for (const close of [...(this.#streams.get(sessionId) ?? [])]) close(reason);\n    44\t  }\n    45\t}\n    46\t\n    47\texport interface SessionServiceOptions {\n    48\t  /**\n    49\t   * Honour `payload.testFault` on inbox rows. Test-only (PI_ORCH_TEST_FAULTS=1): lets the e2e suite kill the\n    50\t   * orchestrator between \"submitted to Pi Durable\" and \"row marked submitted\".\n    51\t   */\n    52\t  testFaults: boolean;\n    53\t  /** Model of a session that predates the per-session model (null in `inbox.sessions`). */\n    54\t  defaultModel: ModelChoice;\n    55\t  /** Model turns one session may use in total. A session that reaches it is `failed`. */\n    56\t  turnBudget: number;\n    57\t  /** Repo workspaces (Phase 4c). Without it a session that asked for a repo is refused at its first input. */\n    58\t  repos?: RepoAccess;\n    59\t}\n    60\t\n    61\t/**\n    62\t * Maps API sessions onto Pi Durable and applies inbox events. One session = one conversation = one\n    63\t * SandboxClaim `pi-conv-<conversation id>` = one PVC; the claim is created lazily by the Harness at the first\n    64\t * tool call, never here.\n    65\t */\n    66\texport class SessionService {\n    67\t  readonly #pool: pg.Pool;\n    68\t  readonly #host: Host;\n    69\t  readonly #options: SessionServiceOptions;\n    70\t  readonly streams = new StreamRegistry();\n    71\t  readonly #creating = new Map<string, Promise<number>>();\n    72\t  readonly #watcher: RunWatcher;\n    73\t\n    74\t  constructor(pool: pg.Pool, host: Host, options: SessionServiceOptions) {\n    75\t    this.#pool = pool;\n    76\t    this.#host = host;\n    77\t    this.#options = options;\n    78\t    this.#watcher = new RunWatcher({\n    79\t      lookup: (conversationId, requestId) => host.submissionState(conversationId, requestId),\n    80\t      onUnanswered: (watched, outcome) => this.#runEnded(watched, outcome),\n    81\t      onError: (error) => {\n    82\t        log(\"run-watch-failed\", { message: errorMessage(error) });\n    83\t      },\n    84\t    });\n    85\t  }\n    86\t\n    87\t  stop(): void {\n    88\t    this.#watcher.stop();\n    89\t  }\n    90\t\n    91\t  /**\n    92\t   * After a start: watch the inputs of live sessions that were handed over recently, because the process that\n    93\t   * handed them over may have died before it saw the run fail. Settled ones drop out at the first poll.\n    94\t   */\n    95\t  async recoverWatches(): Promise<void> {\n    96\t    const { rows } = await this.#pool.query<{\n    97\t      id: string;\n    98\t      session_id: string;\n    99\t      conversation_id: string;\n   100\t    }>(\n   101\t      `select e.id, e.session_id, s.conversation_id\n   102\t         from inbox.events e join inbox.sessions s on s.id = e.session_id\n   103\t        where e.kind in ('message', 'steer') and e.status = 'submitted'\n   104\t          and s.status = 'active' and s.conversation_id is not null\n   105\t          and e.submitted_at > clock_timestamp() - interval '24 hours'\n   106\t        order by e.submitted_at desc limit 1000`,\n   107\t    );\n   108\t    for (const row of rows) {\n   109\t      this.#watcher.add({\n   110\t        sessionId: row.session_id,\n   111\t        conversationId: Number(row.conversation_id),\n   112\t        requestId: row.id,\n   113\t      });\n   114\t    }\n   115\t    if (rows.length > 0) log(\"run-watches-recovered\", { count: rows.length });\n   116\t  }\n   117\t\n   118\t  /**\n   119\t   * A submission ended without an answer. Rejected model credentials and a used-up turn budget end the session\n   120\t   * for good (`failed`); anything else leaves it active. The stored message is ours, never the provider's text.\n   121\t   */\n   122\t  async #runEnded(watched: Watched, outcome: RunOutcome): Promise<void> {\n   123\t    const failure = terminalFailure(outcome);\n   124\t    if (failure === undefined) return;\n   125\t    await this.#failSession(watched.sessionId, watched.conversationId, failure);\n   126\t  }\n   127\t\n   128\t  async #failSession(\n   129\t    sessionId: string,\n   130\t    conversationId: number | null,\n   131\t    failure: string,\n   132\t  ): Promise<void> {\n   133\t    const changed = await failSession(this.#pool, sessionId, failure);\n   134\t    if (!changed) return;\n   135\t    log(\"session-failed\", { session: sessionId, failure });\n   136\t    // Withdraw whatever queued behind the failed run, so nothing more is sent to the provider.\n   137\t    if (conversationId !== null) await this.#host.abort(conversationId);\n   138\t  }\n   139\t\n   140\t  /**\n   141\t   * The session's conversation id, creating the conversation on first use. Serialised per session, so the\n   142\t   * stream handler and the inbox loop cannot create two. A crash between creating the conversation and\n   143\t   * storing its id leaves one empty, unreferenced conversation behind (documented limit).\n   144\t   */\n   145\t  async ensureConversation(session: SessionRow): Promise<number> {\n   146\t    if (session.conversationId !== null) return session.conversationId;\n   147\t    let creating = this.#creating.get(session.id);\n   148\t    if (creating === undefined) {\n   149\t      creating = this.#create(session.id).finally(() => this.#creating.delete(session.id));\n   150\t      this.#creating.set(session.id, creating);\n   151\t    }\n   152\t    return creating;\n   153\t  }\n   154\t\n   155\t  async #create(sessionId: string): Promise<number> {\n   156\t    const current = await getSession(this.#pool, sessionId);\n   157\t    if (current?.conversationId != null) return current.conversationId;\n   158\t    const conversationId = await this.#host.createConversation(\n   159\t      current?.model ?? this.#options.defaultModel,\n   160\t    );\n   161\t    await this.#pool.query(\n   162\t      \"update inbox.sessions set conversation_id = $1 where id = $2 and conversation_id is null\",\n   163\t      [conversationId, sessionId],\n   164\t    );\n   165\t    log(\"conversation-created\", { session: sessionId, conversation: conversationId });\n   166\t    return conversationId;\n   167\t  }\n   168\t\n   169\t  /** Applies one inbox event. Resolves when it is durably handed over; throws PermanentError if it never can be. */\n   170\t  async apply(event: InboxEvent, session: SessionRow): Promise<void> {\n   171\t    if (session.status === \"deleted\") throw new PermanentError(\"session is deleted\");\n   172\t    switch (event.kind) {\n   173\t      case \"message\":\n   174\t      case \"steer\": {\n   175\t        const text = event.payload.text;\n   176\t        if (typeof text !== \"string\" || text === \"\") throw new PermanentError(\"event has no text\");\n   177\t        if (session.status === \"failed\") throw new PermanentError(\"session has failed\");\n   178\t        const conversationId = await this.ensureConversation(session);\n   179\t        await this.#withinBudget(session, conversationId);\n   180\t        // Before the first turn: OneCLI agent, token and clone. A session without a repo skips all of it.\n   181\t        if (session.repo !== null) await this.#prepareRepo(session, conversationId);\n   182\t        const requestId = event.id;\n   183\t        const faultArmed =\n   184\t          this.#options.testFaults && event.payload.testFault === \"exit-after-submit\";\n   185\t        const alreadyAdmitted =\n   186\t          faultArmed && (await this.#host.hasSubmission(conversationId, requestId));\n   187\t        await this.#host.submitInput(conversationId, {\n   188\t          text,\n   189\t          requestId,\n   190\t          steer: event.kind === \"steer\",\n   191\t        });\n   192\t        this.#watcher.add({ sessionId: session.id, conversationId, requestId });\n   193\t        if (faultArmed && !alreadyAdmitted) {\n   194\t          // After the durable hand-over, before the row says so: exactly the window test 4 needs.\n   195\t          // Synchronous write: stdout to a pipe is async and process.exit would drop the line.\n   196\t          writeSync(\n   197\t            1,\n   198\t            `${JSON.stringify({ event: \"test-fault\", fault: \"exit-after-submit\", id: event.id })}\\n`,\n   199\t          );\n   200\t          process.exit(137);\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 9573 {"id":9573,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]","calls":["bash({\"command\":\"cd /workspace/repo && nl -ba packages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts | sed -n '200,340p'; cat docs/session-api.md | grep -in -E 'delet|sourceEventId|owner|size' | head -55; nl -ba packages/session-core/src/store.ts | sed -n '183,229p'; nl -ba packages/ingest/src/events.ts | sed -n '14,40p'; rg 'owner_subject|sourceEventId|requestDelete' packages -g '*.ts' | head -65\"})"]}]}
ENTRY 9577 {"id":9577,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"   200\t          process.exit(137);\n   201\t        }\n   202\t        return;\n   203\t      }\n   204\t      case \"cancel\": {\n   205\t        if (session.conversationId !== null) await this.#host.abort(session.conversationId);\n   206\t        return;\n   207\t      }\n   208\t      case \"delete\": {\n   209\t        await this.#delete(session);\n   210\t        return;\n   211\t      }\n   212\t    }\n   213\t  }\n   214\t\n   215\t  /**\n   216\t   * Provisions the repo session's GitHub access and makes sure its clone exists. What no retry can fix ends the input\n   217\t   * for good (and, for a lost workspace or refused access, the session): the agent must not run a turn in a workspace\n   218\t   * that is not the one the user asked for. Anything else throws as is, so the inbox retries it.\n   219\t   */\n   220\t  async #prepareRepo(session: SessionRow, conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\n   221\t    const repos = this.#options.repos;\n   222\t    if (repos === undefined) throw new PermanentError(\"repository workspaces are not configured\");\n   223\t    try {\n   224\t      await repos.prepare(session, await this.#host.workspaceEnv(conversationId));\n   225\t    } catch (error) {\n   226\t      if (error instanceof WorkspaceLostError) {\n   227\t        await this.#failSession(session.id, conversationId, error.message);\n   228\t        throw new PermanentError(error.message);\n   229\t      }\n   230\t      if (error instanceof GithubDeniedError) {\n   231\t        const failure =\n   232\t          \"GitHub refused access to the repository: is the GitHub App installed on it?\";\n   233\t        await this.#failSession(session.id, conversationId, failure);\n   234\t        throw new PermanentError(failure);\n   235\t      }\n   236\t      if (error instanceof RepoUnavailableError) throw new PermanentError(error.message);\n   237\t      throw error;\n   238\t    }\n   239\t  }\n   240\t\n   241\t  /**\n   242\t   * The per-session turn budget, checked before every input: a session that used all its turns fails for good, and\n   243\t   * otherwise the conversation's `maxTurns` is set to what is left, so a single long run cannot overshoot it.\n   244\t   * Turns are model responses, counted from the stored transcript, so a restart does not reset the count.\n   245\t   */\n   246\t  async #withinBudget(session: SessionRow, conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\n   247\t    const used = await this.#host.turnsUsed(conversationId);\n   248\t    const left = this.#options.turnBudget - used;\n   249\t    if (left <= 0) {\n   250\t      const failure = terminalFailure({ reason: \"turn_limit\" });\n   251\t      await this.#failSession(session.id, conversationId, failure ?? \"turn budget exhausted\");\n   252\t      throw new PermanentError(\"turn budget exhausted\");\n   253\t    }\n   254\t    await this.#host.limitTurns(conversationId, left);\n   255\t  }\n   256\t\n   257\t  /**\n   258\t   * Stop the session, delete the SandboxClaim and PVC, mark the session deleted. The conversation's stored state\n   259\t   * stays: the Postgres adapter can only delete it in a maintenance window (docs/session-api.md).\n   260\t   */\n   261\t  async #delete(session: SessionRow): Promise<void> {\n   262\t    log(\"session-delete-start\", { session: session.id });\n   263\t    // Record what the session holds before anything is revoked, then revoke its OneCLI agent first: from that moment\n   264\t    // its proxy token is dead, whatever happens to the claim after. A plain session has no OneCLI objects.\n   265\t    await writeTombstone(this.#pool, session);\n   266\t    await this.#options.repos?.teardown(session);\n   267\t    const conversationId = session.conversationId;\n   268\t    if (conversationId !== null) {\n   269\t      await this.#host.abort(conversationId);\n   270\t      this.streams.closeSession(session.id, \"deleted\");\n   271\t      await this.#host.destroySandbox(conversationId);\n   272\t    }\n   273\t    await this.#pool.query(\n   274\t      \"update inbox.sessions set status = 'deleted', last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1\",\n   275\t      [session.id],\n   276\t    );\n   277\t    await completeTombstone(this.#pool, session.id);\n   278\t    log(\"session-deleted\", { session: session.id });\n   279\t  }\n   280\t}\n4:reconnect, and delete. It is inbox-shaped: the API writes an event to Postgres and returns; the orchestrator\n11:| `ingest` (`packages/ingest`) | 2, stateless | Authenticates, checks the session owner, writes `inbox.events`, serves `GET /sessions/{id}`, proxies the SSE stream. Keeps accepting events while the orchestrator restarts: its readiness depends on the database only. |\n31:| `POST /sessions` body `{ provider?, model?, repo?, branch? }` | `201 { sessionId, provider, model, reasoning? }` | Creates the session for the caller (the token's owner). No conversation or sandbox yet. The body is optional; without it the session runs the default model. `provider` and `model` go together and must be a pair on the allowlist (see Models), else `400 { \"error\": \"model <provider>/<model> is not allowed\" }`. `repo` (`owner/name` on github.com) and `branch` (optional) give the session a cloned repository workspace, see `docs/repo-workspace.md`; a bad value is `400` and `branch` without `repo` is `400`. The response echoes the model the session will use (and `repo`/`branch`), and the reasoning effort (`reasoning`, from `PI_MODEL_REASONING`; absent when unset). |\n32:| `POST /sessions/{id}/events` body `{ kind, text?, sourceEventId? }` | `202 { eventId, duplicate }` | `kind` is `message`, `steer` or `cancel`. `text` is required for `message` and `steer` (at most 64 KiB). `sourceEventId` (at most 200 characters) deduplicates. `400` invalid body, `409` session is deleting or failed, or the id belongs to another session, `410` session deleted. |\n33:| `GET /sessions/{id}/stream` | `200 text/event-stream` | See Streaming. `503` with `Retry-After` while the orchestrator is down, `410` for a deleted session. |\n34:| `GET /sessions/{id}` | `200 { sessionId, status, model: { provider, model, reasoning? }, failure?, createdAt, lastActivityAt, events: { pending, submitted, failed } }` | Answered from Postgres, so it works while the orchestrator is down. `status` is `active`, `failed`, `deleting` or `deleted`; `failure` is present only when `failed`. A session that predates per-session models reports the default model. |\n35:| `DELETE /sessions/{id}` | `202 { sessionId, status }` | Idempotent. See Deletion. |\n36:| `GET /healthz`, `GET /readyz` | `200` | Both processes. Ingest is ready when the database answers. The orchestrator is ready only once it owns the schema (the Service therefore always points at the owner). |\n39:belongs to another owner**: the two look the same, so the API does not reveal that a session exists.\n41:`DELETE` is also an inbox row (kind `delete`). `POST .../events` with `kind: \"delete\"` is refused; use `DELETE`.\n56:   - `delete`: see Deletion.\n61:- **Deduplication.** `UNIQUE (source, source_event_id)`. `source` is `api:<owner>`. A repeated post returns the\n62:  first event's id with `duplicate: true` and writes nothing. Without a `sourceEventId` every post is its own event.\n69:  batch so later rows cannot overtake it. After 5 attempts (or at once for a permanent error such as a deleted\n86:| `deleted` | none | The session was deleted; the stream ends. |\n113:## Authentication and owners\n115:One middleware, `Authenticator` in `session-core`: it maps request headers to a `Principal { owner }`. Both\n118:- Tokens come from the Kubernetes Secret `api-auth`, key `tokens`, as `owner:token` lines (create it with\n120:- The owner is stored on the session at creation and checked on every call (ingest) and again on the stream\n121:  (orchestrator). A token of another owner gets `404`.\n122:- Test setup creates two owners, `alice` and `bob`.\n140:  stream stay readable, and `DELETE` works. Other model errors (rate limits, network) do not fail the session.\n144:- Session ids are random UUIDs (v4), never sequential. The owner is stored per session as `owner` (the token\n145:  entry's name) and `owner_subject` (the stable identity: `static:<owner>` for static tokens, issuer + subject for\n146:  OIDC later); the owner check compares the subject.\n149:  right name and another or no label is refused, and never deleted by session deletion. (Claims that predate this\n158:  says to delete the claim and its PVC.\n165:  eviction age) is suspended: `Sandbox.spec.operatingMode: Suspended` deletes the Pod and keeps the Sandbox, the claim\n174:- Ingest does not need Kubernetes access. Only the orchestrator ServiceAccount has `delete` on `sandboxclaims` and\n177:## Deletion\n179:`DELETE /sessions/{id}` answers `202` and queues a `delete` row. From that moment new events get `409`; events\n183:2. ends the session's open streams (`deleted`),\n184:3. stops the bridge and deletes the SandboxClaim, then the workspace PVC, and waits until both are gone,\n185:4. marks the session `deleted` (`410` from then on).\n187:**Conversation state is not removed live.** The Postgres adapter's `deleteConversation` is a maintenance helper: it\n188:refuses to run while a storage owns the schema, and Pi Durable 1.5 has no public live-deletion lifecycle. The\n189:session is therefore marked deleted and its conversation rows stay in the `durable` schema until a maintenance job\n190:runs. The job, per `docs/deletion-windows.md` of the adapter:\n192:1. list `inbox.sessions where status = 'deleted' and conversation_id is not null`,\n194:3. with a fresh pool and the same schema configuration, call `deleteConversation(database, conversationId)` for each,\n197:That job is not implemented here. Until it runs, deleted sessions' transcripts remain in Postgres.\n199:A deletion cut off by a crash is safe to repeat: the `delete` row is still pending, and the Kubernetes deletes ignore\n204:What deletion missed is removed by a periodic sweep in the orchestrator (`docs/decisions/0002-orphan-sweep.md`): every\n207:is `deleted` or has no row, and the object is older than `PI_SWEEP_GRACE_SECONDS` (600). At most `PI_SWEEP_MAX_ACTIONS`\n209:never touched, and neither is a session that is `active`, `failed` or `deleting`, even when its sandbox can no longer work.\n225:  is the ConfigMap size (1 MiB); the script refuses a bundle above 900 KB.\n236:  allows one owner.\n237:- Conversation state of deleted sessions stays until the maintenance job.\n   183\t/**\n   184\t * Writes one event and returns. The unique index on (source, source_event_id) makes a repeated post a no-op that\n   185\t * returns the first event's id. The orchestrator is not involved: this works while it is down.\n   186\t */\n   187\texport async function enqueueEvent(\n   188\t  pool: pg.Pool,\n   189\t  event: {\n   190\t    sessionId: string;\n   191\t    source: string;\n   192\t    sourceEventId: string;\n   193\t    kind: EventKind;\n   194\t    payload: InboxEvent[\"payload\"];\n   195\t  },\n   196\t): Promise<EnqueueResult> {\n   197\t  const inserted = await pool.query<{ id: string }>(\n   198\t    `insert into inbox.events (session_id, source, source_event_id, kind, payload)\n   199\t     values ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5)\n   200\t     on conflict (source, source_event_id) do nothing\n   201\t     returning id`,\n   202\t    [event.sessionId, event.source, event.sourceEventId, event.kind, JSON.stringify(event.payload)],\n   203\t  );\n   204\t  const fresh = inserted.rows[0];\n   205\t  if (fresh !== undefined) {\n   206\t    await pool.query(\n   207\t      \"update inbox.sessions set last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1\",\n   208\t      [event.sessionId],\n   209\t    );\n   210\t    return { outcome: \"accepted\", eventId: fresh.id };\n   211\t  }\n   212\t  const { rows } = await pool.query<{ id: string; session_id: string }>(\n   213\t    \"select id, session_id from inbox.events where source = $1 and source_event_id = $2\",\n   214\t    [event.source, event.sourceEventId],\n   215\t  );\n   216\t  const existing = rows[0];\n   217\t  if (existing === undefined || existing.session_id !== event.sessionId) {\n   218\t    return { outcome: \"conflict\" };\n   219\t  }\n   220\t  return { outcome: \"duplicate\", eventId: existing.id };\n   221\t}\n   222\t\n   223\t/** Marks an active session as being deleted, so no further events are accepted. Idempotent. */\n   224\texport async function requestDelete(pool: pg.Pool, sessionId: string): Promise<void> {\n   225\t  await pool.query(\n   226\t    \"update inbox.sessions set status = 'deleting', last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1 and status in ('active', 'failed')\",\n   227\t    [sessionId],\n   228\t  );\n   229\t}\n    14\texport function parseEventBody(body: Record<string, unknown>): ParsedEvent | string {\n    15\t  const { kind, text, sourceEventId } = body;\n    16\t  if (kind === \"delete\") return \"use DELETE /sessions/{id} to delete a session\";\n    17\t  if (kind !== \"message\" && kind !== \"steer\" && kind !== \"cancel\") {\n    18\t    return \"kind must be message, steer or cancel\";\n    19\t  }\n    20\t  if (kind !== \"cancel\") {\n    21\t    if (typeof text !== \"string\" || text.trim() === \"\") return `${kind} needs a non-empty text`;\n    22\t    if (text.length > MAX_TEXT) return `text is longer than ${String(MAX_TEXT)} characters`;\n    23\t  } else if (text !== undefined) {\n    24\t    return \"cancel takes no text\";\n    25\t  }\n    26\t  if (sourceEventId !== undefined) {\n    27\t    if (\n    28\t      typeof sourceEventId !== \"string\" ||\n    29\t      sourceEventId === \"\" ||\n    30\t      sourceEventId.length > MAX_SOURCE_EVENT_ID\n    31\t    ) {\n    32\t      return `sourceEventId must be a string of 1 to ${String(MAX_SOURCE_EVENT_ID)} characters`;\n    33\t    }\n    34\t  }\n    35\t  return {\n    36\t    kind,\n    37\t    payload: typeof text === \"string\" ? { text } : {},\n    38\t    // Without a client-supplied id every post is its own event: there is nothing to deduplicate on.\n    39\t    sourceEventId: typeof sourceEventId === \"string\" ? sourceEventId : `auto-${randomUUID()}`,\n    40\t  };\n/bin/bash: line 1: rg: command not found\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 9593 {"id":9593,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]## Findings\n\n### 1. Client event IDs can prevent session deletion\n- Severity: high\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/ingest/src/server.ts:227\n- What happens: An owner can post an event with `sourceEventId` equal to `delete:<session-id>`, then delete that session. The delete enqueue is treated as a duplicate of the earlier event, but the session is still marked `deleting`. No delete event exists to revoke credentials or remove the sandbox, and repeated DELETE requests cannot fix it. The same ID used in another session produces a conflict with the same result.\n- Evidence: DELETE uses `sourceEventId: \\`delete:${session.id}\\`` and then calls `requestDelete` even when enqueue returns a conflict. Client-supplied IDs are not reserved, and deduplication checks only source, ID and session—not event kind.\n- Fix idea: Put internal delete events in a separate deduplication namespace from client events. Only mark the session deleting when a genuine delete event has been inserted or verified.\n\n### 2. Event admission races with deletion\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/ingest/src/server.ts:81\n- What happens: A POST can load an active session and then wait while its body is sent. A concurrent DELETE can queue and complete deletion before that POST resumes. The POST still uses its stale session status, inserts an event, and returns 202, although the orchestrator subsequently rejects the event because the session is deleted.\n- Evidence: The route loads `session` before reading the body; `postEvent` later checks `session.status !== \"active\"` and calls `enqueueEvent`, whose insert has no current-status condition.\n- Fix idea: Serialize event admission and deletion using a transaction and session-row lock, checking the current status while inserting. Queue the delete and change the status atomically under the same lock.\n\n### 3. A temporarily failing deletion becomes permanently unretryable\n- Severity: high\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/orchestrator/src/inbox.ts:177\n- What happens: If teardown fails five times—for example, because Kubernetes or OneCLI is temporarily unavailable—the delete event is marked failed. The session remains `deleting`, potentially retaining its sandbox or credentials. A later DELETE is deduplicated against that failed event rather than requeued, so recovery of the dependency does not complete cleanup.\n- Evidence: The inbox marks an event permanent when `attempt >= MAX_ATTEMPTS`; DELETE always reuses `delete:${session.id}`, and `enqueueEvent` returns the existing event as a duplicate regardless of its status.\n- Fix idea: Retry cleanup until it succeeds, with bounded backoff and alerting, or allow a subsequent DELETE to requeue a failed delete event safely.\n\n## Areas checked with no findings\n- Authentication and owner checks on ingest routes and the orchestrator stream route.\n- Constant-time static-token comparison.\n- SQL parameterization and migration ordering.\n- Repository and branch validation, JSON body size limits, and generic server error responses.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
